MC.addO({"enchants:mechanics/blockdrops":{"h":"<h2>BlockDrops</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Rebuilds a broken block&#x27;s drops using the player&#x27;s real held tool. Because drops are recomputed from the live <code>ItemStack</code>, vanilla enchantment effects on the tool — Silk Touch, Fortune, and any MythicEnchants custom enchants — are applied exactly as they would be during a normal break.</p>\n<p>Use this on <code>~onBlockBreak</code> to implement Fortune-style or Silk-Touch-style behavior. An optional block-type filter limits the mechanic to specific blocks or block tags. Drop amounts can be scaled with a configurable multiplier range, and a chance parameter lets the mechanic fire probabilistically.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>exp</code></td><td><code>experience</code>, <code>xp</code></td><td>Whether the block drops XP</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>blocktypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>blocks</code></td><td>Comma-separated block tags (<code>#minecraft:coal_ores</code>), material names (<code>NETHER_QUARTZ_ORE</code>), and/or <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> custom-block ids. Empty means all blocks (including any custom block).</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (all blocks)</td></tr><tr><td><code>chance</code></td><td></td><td>Probability <code>[0.0–1.0]</code> that the mechanic produces drops at all. Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code>.</td><td><code>1.0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>mult</code></td><td><code>multiplier</code>, <code>m</code></td><td>Drop amount multiplier. Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code> and <code>min..max</code> range syntax. When a range is given, a random value in <code>[min, max)</code> is picked each cast and the result is rounded to the nearest integer (minimum 1).</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>multmin</code></td><td><code>mmin</code></td><td>Explicit range minimum. Overrides the left side of <code>mult=min..max</code>. Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code>.</td><td><i>(from <code>mult</code>)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>multmax</code></td><td><code>mmax</code></td><td>Explicit range maximum. Overrides the right side of <code>mult=min..max</code>. Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code>.</td><td><i>(from <code>mult</code>)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>savecontainer</code></td><td><code>keepcontainer</code>, <code>savecontents</code></td><td>When the broken block is a non-shulker container (chest, barrel, furnace, hopper, dispenser, dropper, etc.) with items in it, save those contents onto the dropped container item&#x27;s PDC instead of spilling them on the ground.</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>silkspawner</code></td><td></td><td>When the broken block is a mob spawner, drop a spawner item that carries the exact spawner <code>BlockState</code> (entity type, spawn delay/count/range, potential-spawn table, and any custom PDC) via <code>BlockStateMeta</code>. Vanilla spawners never drop themselves — this is what makes silk-touching one possible at all. <code>chance</code> also gates this roll specifically — see <span class=\"ilink\">Silk Spawner</span> below.</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>spawneruses</code></td><td><code>spawnercharges</code></td><td><code>spawnerusemode=CHARGES</code> only: limits how many spawners this <code>silkspawner</code> enchant can mine before it removes itself from the tool. <code>-1</code> = unlimited.</td><td><code>-1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>spawnerusemode</code></td><td></td><td><code>CHARGES</code> (default) uses the <code>spawneruses</code> PDC-counter above. <code>LEVEL</code> instead decrements the firing enchantment&#x27;s own level on the tool by 1 per successful mine, soulbound-style, removing the enchant once its level hits 0. <code>spawneruses</code> is ignored in this mode.</td><td><code>CHARGES</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>silktouch</code></td><td></td><td>Forces silk-touch-style drops (the block itself, e.g. <code>STONE</code> not <code>COBBLESTONE</code>) regardless of whether the tool actually carries a vanilla Silk Touch level. Implemented by casting drops against a cloned tool with a real Silk Touch enchant added (Fortune removed from that clone to avoid the vanilla conflict) — so block-specific silk-touch drop rules (glass, ice, spawners via a normal break, etc.) are handled exactly like vanilla. Combines with <code>mult</code>.</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Container Contents</h3>\n<p>When <code>savecontainer=true</code> and the broken block is a <code>Container</code> other than a shulker box (chest, barrel, furnace, hopper, dispenser, dropper, etc.) and it has non-air items in its inventory:</p>\n<ul><li>The contents are <b>not</b> spilled onto the ground.</li><li>They are serialized onto the PDC of the dropped item that matches the broken block&#x27;s own material (e.g. breaking a chest attaches its contents to the dropped <code>CHEST</code> item) — the same technique vanilla uses to keep a shulker box&#x27;s items inside the box item itself.</li><li>A separate listener (<code>ContainerContentsRestoreListener</code>) reads that PDC back off whenever the item is placed as a block and, if the placed block is a <code>Container</code>, restores the saved contents into its inventory.</li></ul>\n<p>This works regardless of where the item travels in the meantime (player inventory, dropped on the ground, hoppers, item frames, shulker boxes, etc.) — the data lives on the item itself, not the original block location, so there&#x27;s no requirement to place it back in the same spot.</p>\n<p>Shulker boxes are always skipped by this option (and don&#x27;t need it): Bukkit already preserves a shulker box&#x27;s contents in its dropped item&#x27;s <code>BlockStateMeta</code> natively, independent of location, exactly like the mechanism above.</p>\n<p>If the container has no contents, or <code>savecontainer</code> is unset/<code>false</code>, contents spill onto the ground as before.</p>\n<h3>Silk Spawner</h3>\n<p>Setting <code>silkspawner=true</code> lets an enchant &quot;silk touch&quot; a mob spawner — something vanilla never allows, silk touch or not. When the broken block is a <code>CreatureSpawner</code>:</p>\n<ul><li><code>chance</code> is rolled to decide whether the attempt succeeds. Since a spawner block has no other vanilla drops, this doubles as both &quot;does the mechanic do anything&quot; and &quot;does the spawner item drop&quot; — a failed roll simply produces no spawner item (and, per the mechanic&#x27;s normal early-return, no charge/level is spent either).</li><li>On success, a <code>Material.SPAWNER</code> item is added to the drops, with its <code>BlockStateMeta</code> set to the exact broken spawner&#x27;s <code>BlockState</code> — this preserves the spawned entity type, spawn delay/count/nearby-range, the potential-spawn table, and any custom PDC on the block.</li><li>The item is exempt from the <code>mult</code> multiplier (it&#x27;s always a single spawner, not a stack that scales).</li><li>Placing that item back down recreates a spawner block with all of the above restored, via vanilla&#x27;s own tile-entity-from-item placement — no companion listener is needed for this part.</li></ul>\n<h4>Limited Uses (<code>spawnerusemode</code>)</h4>\n<p>By default <code>silkspawner</code> has unlimited uses. Two mutually exclusive modes cap it:</p>\n<p><b><code>spawnerusemode=CHARGES</code></b> (default) — <code>spawneruses=N</code> (or the <code>spawnercharges</code> alias) caps how many spawners a single enchanted tool can mine:</p>\n<ul><li>The remaining-charge count is stored on the <b>tool&#x27;s own PDC</b>, not the player or the world. It&#x27;s seeded from <code>spawneruses</code> the first time the enchant successfully silk-touches a spawner on that tool, then decremented by 1 on every subsequent successful mine.</li><li>When the counter reaches <code>0</code>, the enchantment responsible for the cast (resolved from the active <code>CastingContext</code>, the same way <code>RecoverItemMechanic</code>&#x27;s use-limit works) is <b>removed from the tool</b>, and the charge PDC key is cleaned up.</li><li><code>spawneruses=-1</code> (the default) disables the charge system entirely — unlimited spawner mining.</li></ul>\n<p><b><code>spawnerusemode=LEVEL</code></b> — soulbound-style: the enchant&#x27;s own level on the tool IS the remaining-uses counter (mirrors <code>RecoverItemMechanic</code>&#x27;s <code>uselevels</code> mode). A level-3 silk-spawner enchant can mine 3 spawners; each successful mine reduces the level by 1 (<code>meta.addEnchant(enchantment, newLevel, true)</code>), and reaching level 0 removes the enchant entirely. <code>spawneruses</code>/<code>spawnercharges</code> is ignored in this mode — the enchant&#x27;s level, set however it was enchanted/applied, is the only knob.</p>\n<p>In both modes, the enchant being fully removed (not just disabled) means the tool can be re-enchanted with the same silk-spawner enchant afterward for a fresh set of uses — it isn&#x27;t permanently spent.</p>\n<h3>Block Matching</h3>\n<p>Each entry in <code>bt</code> is resolved at load time:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Example</th><th>Resolves as</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>#namespace:tag</code></td><td><code>#minecraft:coal_ores</code></td><td>Bukkit block tag — matches all tagged materials</td></tr><tr><td><code>#tag</code> (no namespace)</td><td><code>#coal_ores</code></td><td>Shorthand — <code>minecraft:</code> namespace is assumed</td></tr><tr><td><code>MATERIAL</code></td><td><code>NETHER_QUARTZ_ORE</code></td><td>Exact Bukkit <code>Material</code> match</td></tr><tr><td><code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>nexo:ruby_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific Nexo custom block by its item id</td></tr><tr><td><code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>crucible:sapphire_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific MythicCrucible custom block by its internal item id</td></tr><tr><td><code>mythic:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>mythic:sapphire_ore</code></td><td>Alias for <code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code> — Crucible blocks are MythicMobs-native</td></tr><tr><td><code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>itemsadder:topaz_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific ItemsAdder custom block by its namespaced id</td></tr><tr><td><code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>craftengine:emerald_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific CraftEngine custom block by its namespaced id</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Unknown tags and materials log a warning at startup and are silently skipped at runtime. An empty <code>bt</code> matches everything, including any custom block encountered.</p>\n<h3>Custom Blocks</h3>\n<p>Nexo, MythicCrucible, ItemsAdder, and CraftEngine custom blocks are noteblock/mushroom/tripwire/chorus &quot;carrier&quot; blocks (or, for ItemsAdder/CraftEngine, their own block-identity mechanisms) with an internal addon-side id — they have no meaningful vanilla drops of their own (<code>block.getDrops(tool)</code> on the carrier material would return nonsense, like a plain note-block item). <code>blockdrops</code> detects these automatically and pulls from that addon&#x27;s own configured loot instead:</p>\n<ul><li><b>Nexo</b> — reads the block&#x27;s <code>Breakable.getDrop()</code> config, respecting its own silktouch/fortune/tool-requirement rules, via the published <code>com.nexomc:nexo</code> API (no reflection).</li><li><b>MythicCrucible</b> — reads the block&#x27;s MythicMobs <code>DropTable</code> (reached via reflection, since Crucible ships no public API jar for its custom-block registry) and generates/spawns from it directly.</li><li><b>ItemsAdder</b> — reads the block&#x27;s configured loot via <code>CustomBlock.getLoot(tool, false)</code>, using the published <code>com.github.LoneDev6:api-itemsadder</code> API (no reflection).</li><li><b>CraftEngine</b> — reads the block&#x27;s own loot table via <code>ImmutableBlockState.getDrops(...)</code>, with the held tool injected into the loot context, using the published <code>net.momirealms:craft-engine-core</code>/<code>-bukkit</code> API (no reflection). CraftEngine exposes no silk-touch-style flag on its loot API — whatever tool-conditional behavior a pack author configured is opaque to us; passing the tool into context is the only lever available.</li></ul>\n<p>In all cases <code>mult</code>/<code>chance</code>/<code>exp</code> still apply on top of the addon&#x27;s own drop output. <code>silktouch</code> has <b>no effect</b> on a MythicCrucible block&#x27;s own harvest-tool gate — that gate is evaluated earlier (in <code>BlockInteractTrigger.preemptCustomBlock</code> / <code>VeinMinerMechanic</code>, before any mechanic on the skill line has even resolved), so this parameter cannot retroactively bypass it. Nexo blocks are unaffected either way — they report their own silktouch flag from their <code>Drop</code> config. ItemsAdder and CraftEngine blocks have no equivalent tool gate exposed to us.</p>\n<p>Because Nexo/Crucible/ItemsAdder/CraftEngine&#x27;s own <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> listeners would otherwise spawn their configured loot <i>before</i> <code>blockdrops</code> (or any enchant mechanic) ever gets a chance to run, taking over a custom-block break only happens when the wielded tool actually has an enabled enchant registered for <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> — a plain tool with no relevant enchant leaves the addon&#x27;s normal behavior completely untouched. See <code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> in the trigger reference for the dedicated custom-block-only trigger.</p>\n<h4><code>?customblock</code> Condition</h4>\n<p>A standalone MythicMobs condition (aliases: <code>?custblock</code>, <code>?iscustomblock</code>) for gating <i>any</i> mechanic — not just the drop mechanics above — on whether the current block-break&#x27;s block is a custom block. Reads from the same <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> context as <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>veinminer</code>/etc., so it only evaluates meaningfully inside a <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onStartdestroyblock</code> skill line.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>addon</code></td><td><code>a</code>, <code>source</code></td><td>Restrict to one addon: <code>nexo</code>, <code>crucible</code>, <code>itemsadder</code>, or <code>craftengine</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (any addon)</td></tr><tr><td><code>blocktypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>ids</code></td><td>Comma-separated <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries — matches a specific custom block by id, same syntax as <code>blockdrops{bt=...}</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (any custom block)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Any custom block, any addon\n- particle{p=totem;a=10} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock\n\n# Only Nexo custom blocks\n- sound{s=block.amethyst_block.chime} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock{addon=nexo}\n\n# A specific MythicCrucible ore\n- effect:message{m=&quot;&lt;gold&gt;You struck sapphire!&quot;} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock{bt=crucible:sapphire_ore}</code></pre>\n<h3>Multiplier Range</h3>\n<p><code>mult=min..max</code> picks a continuous random value in <code>[min, max)</code> and rounds it to the nearest integer (floored at 1). This lets you model discrete vanilla-style multipliers:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Expression</th><th>Effective integer range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mult=1</code></td><td>always ×1 (no change)</td></tr><tr><td><code>mult=1..3</code></td><td>×1 or ×2</td></tr><tr><td><code>mult=2</code></td><td>always ×2</td></tr><tr><td><code>mult=&lt;math:enchant_level&gt;</code></td><td>fixed ×level</td></tr><tr><td><code>mult=1..&lt;math:enchant_level+2&gt;</code></td><td>×1 through ×(level+1) — for custom extra scaling</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Vanilla Silk Touch — drops the block itself, suppresses XP\n# NOTE: silktouch=true is required — without it, blockdrops respects the tool&#x27;s REAL\n# enchantments, so a tool with no actual Silk Touch level still drops e.g. COBBLESTONE.\nsilk_touch:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{exp=false;silktouch=true} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Vanilla Fortune — ores only; mult controls the drop multiplier directly (base drops × mult)\nfortune:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=#minecraft:coal_ores,#minecraft:iron_ores,#minecraft:diamond_ores;mult=1..&lt;math:enchant_level+2&gt;} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Fixed ×3 multiplier on all blocks — no filter\ntriple_harvest:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{mult=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# 50% chance to double drops from crops only\nharvest_luck:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=#minecraft:crops;chance=0.5;mult=2} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Level-scaled chance: 10% per level\nlucky_strike:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=#minecraft:coal_ores;chance=&lt;math:enchant_level*0.1&gt;;mult=2} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Double drops from a specific Nexo custom ore, triple from a Crucible one, quadruple from ItemsAdder\ncustom_ore_fortune:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=nexo:ruby_ore;mult=2} @self ~onBlockBreak\n    - blockdrops{bt=crucible:sapphire_ore;mult=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n    - blockdrops{bt=itemsadder:topaz_ore;mult=4} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Silk Touch that also keeps a container&#x27;s contents in the dropped item\ncontainer_silk_touch:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{exp=false;silktouch=true;savecontainer=true} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Silk-touch a mob spawner, unlimited uses\nsilk_spawner:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=SPAWNER;exp=false;silkspawner=true} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Silk-touch spawners, but only 5 times before the enchant removes itself from the tool\nlimited_silk_spawner:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=SPAWNER;exp=false;silkspawner=true;spawneruses=5} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Soulbound-style: the enchant&#x27;s own level is the remaining-uses counter (level 3 = 3 mines)\nsoulbound_silk_spawner:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=SPAWNER;exp=false;silkspawner=true;spawnerusemode=LEVEL} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# 25% chance per attempt to successfully silk-touch a spawner, unlimited attempts otherwise\nrisky_silk_spawner:\n  Skills:\n    - blockdrops{bt=SPAWNER;exp=false;silkspawner=true;chance=0.25} @self ~onBlockBreak</code></pre>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>The mechanic calls <code>event.setDropItems(false)</code> before spawning its own drops, so vanilla drops are suppressed and replaced cleanly. If the mechanic returns early (block type mismatch, chance roll failed, no tool), <code>setDropItems</code> is <b>not</b> called and vanilla behavior is preserved.</li><li>Computed drops are spawned as real <code>Item</code> entities and passed through a genuine <code>BlockDropItemEvent</code> (the same event vanilla fires for a natural break), rather than being placed in the world directly. This means bonus-drop plugins that listen on that event — mcMMO&#x27;s Mining double drops, Excavation treasure, Woodcutting/Herbalism bonuses, etc. — see these as natural drops and apply their own bonuses on top, exactly as they would for a vanilla break. If another plugin cancels the event, the spawned items are removed and nothing is left in the world.</li><li>When <code>exp=false</code> the event&#x27;s XP-to-drop is set to <code>0</code>. When <code>exp=true</code> (the default) vanilla XP is left untouched.</li><li>Drop computation picks one of three tools to pass to <code>block.getDrops(...)</code>, in priority order: <code>silktouch=true</code> → a clone with a real Silk Touch enchant forced on (Fortune stripped from that clone); else <code>mult != 1</code> → a clone with Fortune and Silk Touch stripped, so the configured multiplier is the sole source of quantity scaling with no double-dipping; else (default) the real tool, so its own Fortune/Silk Touch apply natively.</li><li>The multiplier applies to each <code>ItemStack</code>&#x27;s <code>amount</code>, rounded with <code>Math.round</code> and clamped to a minimum of <code>1</code>. It does not duplicate stacks — a single diamond ore that Fortune would give 3 diamonds produces a single stack of 3.</li><li>Tool resolution is direct: the mechanic reads <code>player.getInventory().getItemInMainHand()</code> from the live <code>BlockBreakEvent</code>, guaranteeing the exact <code>ItemStack</code> (with all components/NBT) Paper used for the break.</li><li><code>savecontainer</code> and <code>silkspawner</code> are independent — a spawner is never a <code>Container</code>, so the two options don&#x27;t interact even when both are set on the same enchant.</li><li><code>chance</code> is a single early-return gate for the whole cast, not spawner-specific — if <code>blocktypes</code> includes non-spawner blocks alongside spawners, a failed roll skips drop rebuilding for those blocks too, not just the spawner roll. Scope <code>blocktypes</code> to <code>SPAWNER</code> alone (as in the examples above) if you want <code>chance</code> to read purely as &quot;chance to successfully silk-touch a spawner.&quot;</li></ul>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>blockdrops</code></li><li><code>tooldrops</code></li><li><code>vanillablockdrops</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/breakblockaction":{"h":"<h2>BreakBlockAction</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Breaks the block at the target location — same parameters and contract as MythicMobs&#x27; own <code>breakBlock</code>/<code>blockBreak</code> mechanic, but spawns drops through the real <code>BlockDropItemEvent</code> pipeline instead of a raw <code>Block.breakNaturally()</code> call.</p>\n<p>Use this as a drop-in replacement for <code>breakBlock</code> on any skill line that breaks a block the player didn&#x27;t directly mine themselves — most commonly a tunneling/multi-break enchant that fires several breaks off one swing via <code>@targetblock</code>.</p>\n<h3>Why this exists</h3>\n<p>MythicMobs&#x27; <code>breakBlock</code> calls <code>Block.breakNaturally(tool)</code>, which computes and spawns drops internally and <b>never fires <code>BlockDropItemEvent</code></b>.</p>\n<p>Third-party bonus-drop / ore-luck plugins (AuraSkills&#x27; Mining Luck, mcMMO&#x27;s double drops, etc.) hook <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> at <code>MONITOR</code> priority and re-query <code>block.getDrops()</code> <b>live from the still-standing block</b>. That only works for a normal player break because Bukkit fires all <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> listeners — including MONITOR ones — before the block is actually removed.</p>\n<p><code>breakBlock</code> doesn&#x27;t follow that order: it fires the event, then calls <code>breakNaturally()</code> inline in the same method, before returning control to Bukkit&#x27;s dispatcher. By the time a MONITOR-priority listener runs, the block is already air, so its drop re-query comes back empty and the bonus silently never applies — even though the event technically fired.</p>\n<p><code>breakblockaction</code> fixes this by computing drops once (<code>block.getDrops(tool, player)</code>) before removing the block, then spawning them through <code>MechanicSupport.dropWithVanillaEvent</code>, which fires a genuine <code>BlockDropItemEvent</code> with the drops already in the world as real item entities — exactly like a natural player break, and exactly what those plugins expect to see.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>dodrops</code></td><td><code>drops</code>, <code>d</code></td><td>Whether to drop items from the broken block</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>doeffect</code></td><td><code>effect</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>Whether to play the block-break particle/sound effect</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>usetool</code></td><td><code>tool</code>, <code>t</code></td><td>Use the caster&#x27;s held main-hand item for Fortune/Silk Touch when computing drops</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>ignoreblocks</code></td><td><code>ignore</code>, <code>ib</code></td><td>Comma-separated block tags (<code>#minecraft:...</code>), materials, and/or <code>*substring</code> wildcards to skip entirely — no break, no drops, no event. Same syntax as <code>veinminer</code>&#x27;s <code>t=</code> filter, plus <code>*foo</code> (see <span class=\"ilink\">Wildcard Matching</span>).</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (no filter)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Tunnel enchant — break the block directly ahead of the player\ntunnel_forward:\n  Skills:\n    - breakblockaction @targetblock{y=1}\n    - breakblockaction @targetblock{y=-1}\n\n# No effect, tool-based drops still apply\nquiet_tunnel:\n  Skills:\n    - breakblockaction{effect=false} @targetblock{x=1}\n\n# Tunnel that skips obsidian and any wither-immune block tagged for it\ntunnel_no_obsidian:\n  Skills:\n    - breakblockaction{ignoreblocks=OBSIDIAN,#minecraft:wither_immune} @targetblock{y=1}\n\n# Same, using the wildcard shorthand instead of the exact tag key\ntunnel_no_obsidian_wildcard:\n  Skills:\n    - breakblockaction{ignoreblocks=OBSIDIAN,*wither_immune} @targetblock{y=1}</code></pre>\n<h3>Custom Blocks</h3>\n<p>Nexo, MythicCrucible, ItemsAdder, and CraftEngine custom blocks (noteblock/mushroom/tripwire/chorus carriers with no meaningful vanilla drops of their own) are detected automatically and routed through that addon&#x27;s own loot config instead of <code>block.getDrops()</code> — same mechanism <code>veinminer</code> uses. A real <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> is never published for these blocks; <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> are dispatched directly in-process instead, so other enchants on the tool (<code>blockdrops</code>, <code>fakedrops</code>, etc.) still react normally and can claim the drops ahead of the addon&#x27;s own loot.</p>\n<h3>Wildcard Matching</h3>\n<p><code>ignoreblocks</code> entries starting with <code>*</code> are a fuzzy match, not real MythicMobs/Bukkit syntax — a convenience for porting configs from other plugins (e.g. See&#x27;s <code>*wither_immune</code>) without needing to know the exact tag key. <code>*foo</code> matches any block whose type name contains <code>foo</code> (e.g. <code>*_ore</code> matches every <code>..._ORE</code> material) <b>or</b> whose <code>minecraft:foo</code> tag contains the block. Prefer the real <code>#minecraft:...</code> tag syntax when you know it — it&#x27;s more precise and doesn&#x27;t depend on naming coincidences.</p>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>Only a real <code>Player</code> caster triggers the synthetic <code>BlockBreakEvent</code>/custom-block dispatch and protection-plugin check, matching <code>breakBlock</code>&#x27;s own behavior — a non-player caster breaks the block directly with no event, no custom-block handling, and no tool-based drops.</li><li><code>usetool=false</code> computes drops from an empty hand (no Fortune/Silk Touch), same as <code>breakBlock{usetool=false}</code>.</li><li>Does not dispatch <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> for the vanilla-block path (only for custom blocks, to let <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>fakedrops</code> claim their drops) and has no vein-radius handling — for that, chain multiple <code>breakblockaction</code>/<code>@targetblock</code> lines or use <code>veinminer</code> itself. <code>breakblockaction</code> is intentionally the minimal fix for <code>breakBlock</code>&#x27;s drop-event gap, not a <code>veinminer</code> replacement.</li><li>An unknown tag or material in <code>ignoreblocks</code> logs a load-time warning and is otherwise ignored; an empty <code>*</code> wildcard (just <code>*</code>) also warns and is ignored.</li><li>Attached-block physics drops (torches, rails, redstone dust knocked off as a side effect) are <b>not</b> snapshotted/preserved the way <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>veinminer</code> do — this mirrors <code>breakBlock</code>&#x27;s own behavior exactly, including that gap.</li></ul>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>breakblockaction</code></li><li><code>realbreakblock</code></li><li><code>breaktargetblock</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/counter":{"h":"<h2>Counter</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>A generic named counter for tracking arbitrary resources/stats — kill counts, soul shards, ability charges, streaks, anything you&#x27;d otherwise need a companion plugin for.</p>\n<p>A counter is a persistent value stored under a key derived from the counter&#x27;s <code>key=</code> name, with an optional expiry:</p>\n<ul><li><b><code>scope=player</code></b> (default) — stored on the player. Survives a server restart.</li><li><b><code>scope=item</code></b> — stored on the resolved item. Travels with the item: trading, dropping, storing in a container, or moving it between inventories all keep the counter intact.</li></ul>\n<p>An expired counter is deleted the next time anything reads or writes it — there&#x27;s no separate cleanup step to run.</p>\n<p>Four pieces make up the feature:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Piece</th><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mechanic</td><td><code>addcounter</code> (aliases <code>counter</code>, <code>modifycounter</code>, <code>removecounter</code>)</td><td>Add to / set / remove a counter&#x27;s value</td></tr><tr><td>Condition</td><td><code>?counter</code> (aliases <code>hascounter</code>, <code>checkcounter</code>)</td><td>Check a counter&#x27;s value against a range</td></tr><tr><td>PlaceholderAPI</td><td><code>%mythicenchants_counter_&lt;key&gt;%</code> / <code>%mythicenchants_counter_item_&lt;slot&gt;_&lt;key&gt;%</code></td><td>Read a counter&#x27;s value into text/GUIs/other plugins</td></tr><tr><td>MythicMobs placeholder</td><td><code>&lt;counter.KEY&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;counter.item.SLOT.KEY&gt;</code></td><td>Read a counter&#x27;s value directly inside skill lines/config strings</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Mechanic: <code>addcounter</code></h3>\n<h4>Attributes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code></td><td>The counter&#x27;s name. Sanitized to <code>[a-z0-9/_.-]</code> when building the storage key, so any casing/characters are safe to pass in. <b>Required</b> — an empty/missing key makes the mechanic no-op (<code>INVALID_CONFIG</code>).</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>val</code>, <code>v</code></td><td>Amount to add (mode <code>add</code>) or the exact value to write (mode <code>set</code>). Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code> and placeholders. Rounded to the nearest <code>long</code>.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>m</code></td><td><code>add</code>, <code>set</code>, or <code>remove</code>. If omitted, the <b>mechanic name itself</b> sets the default: <code>addcounter{...}</code> defaults to <code>add</code>, <code>removecounter{...}</code> defaults to <code>remove</code>. An explicit <code>mode=</code> always overrides the name-based default.</td><td>see above</td></tr><tr><td><code>scope</code></td><td><code>sc</code></td><td><code>player</code> or <code>item</code>.</td><td><code>player</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>expiry</code></td><td><code>expires</code>, <code>duration</code>, <code>d</code></td><td>How long the counter stays valid, as <code>&lt;n&gt;t</code> (ticks), <code>&lt;n&gt;s</code> (seconds, ×20 internally), or <code>-1</code>/<code>never</code>/<code>forever</code> for no expiry. Every <code>add</code>/<code>set</code> <b>refreshes</b> the expiry to this value — it does not stack with a previous deadline.</td><td><code>-1</code> (never expires)</td></tr><tr><td><code>slot</code></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>Equipment slot to target when <code>scope=item</code>, or <code>TRIGGER</code> for the item that fired the enchant. Ignored when <code>scope=player</code>.</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>min</code></td><td>—</td><td>Optional floor. If the result of an <code>add</code>/<code>set</code> falls below <code>min</code>, it&#x27;s clamped up to <code>min</code> (and the clamped value is what&#x27;s actually stored).</td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td><code>max</code></td><td>—</td><td>Optional ceiling, same clamping behavior as <code>min</code>.</td><td>none</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Item Resolution</h4>\n<p><code>slot=TRIGGER</code> (the default) resolves to the item that fired the enchant, falling back to the entity&#x27;s main hand. An explicit slot name (<code>HEAD</code>, <code>OFFHAND</code>, …) reads that equipment slot directly.</p>\n<h4>Examples</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Track soul kills on the player, no expiry — persists across restarts\nsoul_reaper:\n  Skills:\n    - addcounter{key=soulkills;amt=1} @self ~onKillPlayer\n\n# Same, but the counter resets itself 125 seconds after the last kill\nsoul_reaper_streak:\n  Skills:\n    - addcounter{key=soulkills;amt=1;expiry=2500t} @self ~onKillPlayer\n    # or equivalently: expiry=125s\n\n# Limited-charge item: consume a charge on use, floor at 0\ncharged_wand:\n  Skills:\n    - addcounter{key=charges;amt=-1;scope=item;min=0} @self ~onUse ?counter{key=charges;value=&gt;0;scope=item}\n\n# Stamp starting charges onto the item when the enchant is applied\ncharged_wand_init:\n  Skills:\n    - addcounter{key=charges;mode=set;amt=5;scope=item} @self ~onEnchantApply\n\n# Explicit remove\nreset_streak:\n  Skills:\n    - removecounter{key=soulkills;scope=player} @self ~onDeath</code></pre>\n<h4>Aliases</h4>\n<ul><li><code>addcounter</code></li><li><code>counter</code></li><li><code>modifycounter</code></li><li><code>removecounter</code></li></ul>\n<h4>Notes</h4>\n<ul><li>Works with <code>@self</code>, <code>@trigger</code>, or any entity targeter; with no target it falls back to the caster.</li><li><code>scope=player</code> requires the resolved entity to be a real player — on a mob or other non-player entity it fails silently (no counter is written).</li><li><code>scope=item</code> changes are visible to conditions/placeholders immediately, same tick.</li><li>If an <code>add</code>/<code>set</code> brings a counter&#x27;s value to exactly <code>0</code>, it&#x27;s removed entirely rather than stored as a zero — reading it back still gives <code>0</code>, it just doesn&#x27;t linger as leftover data once it&#x27;s back at baseline.</li><li>Debug logging (<code>/mench debug</code>) prints each add/set/remove with the resolved key and resulting value.</li></ul>\n<h3>Condition: <code>?counter</code></h3>\n<h4>Attributes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code></td><td>Counter name to check.</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>val</code>, <code>v</code></td><td>Range expression: exact (<code>5</code>), comparison (<code>&gt;=5</code>, <code>&lt;10</code>), or inclusive range (<code>5-10</code>, <code>5to10</code>).</td><td><code>&gt;0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>scope</code></td><td><code>sc</code></td><td><code>player</code> or <code>item</code>.</td><td><code>player</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>slot</code></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>Equipment slot when <code>scope=item</code>, or <code>TRIGGER</code>.</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>An absent or expired counter reads as <code>0</code> — so <code>?counter{key=charges;value=&gt;0;scope=item}</code> naturally fails once a charge-limited item runs out, with no separate existence check needed.</p>\n<h4>Examples</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>- ?counter{key=soulkills;value=&gt;=5}                     # player-scoped, default\n- ?counter{key=soulkills;value=&gt;=5;scope=player}\n- ?counter{key=charges;value=&gt;0;scope=item}              # item-scoped, TRIGGER slot\n- ?counter{key=charges;value=0;scope=item;slot=offhand}</code></pre>\n<h4>Aliases</h4>\n<ul><li><code>counter</code></li><li><code>hascounter</code></li><li><code>checkcounter</code></li></ul>\n<h3>Placeholders</h3>\n<p>Two independent placeholder systems expose counters — pick whichever fits where you&#x27;re reading the value from.</p>\n<h4>PlaceholderAPI (<code>%...%</code>)</h4>\n<p>Available as both <code>%mythicenchants_...%</code> and <code>%mench_...%</code>. Use these outside skill lines — GUI titles/lore, chat formats, scoreboards, other plugins.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Description</th><th>Online-only</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>counter_&lt;key&gt;</code></td><td>Value of a player-scoped counter for the placeholder&#x27;s player</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><code>counter_item_&lt;slot&gt;_&lt;key&gt;</code></td><td>Value of an item-scoped counter on <code>&lt;slot&gt;</code> for the placeholder&#x27;s player</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Slots for <code>counter_item_...</code> use the same names as the existing slot-based placeholders: <code>mainhand</code>/<code>hand</code>, <code>offhand</code>, <code>head</code>/<code>helm</code>, <code>chest</code>, <code>legs</code>, <code>feet</code>/<code>boots</code>.</p>\n<p>Both return <code>&quot;0&quot;</code> if the player is offline, the counter doesn&#x27;t exist, it has expired, or (for the item form) the slot is empty.</p>\n<p>Examples: <code>%mythicenchants_counter_soulkills%</code>, <code>%mench_counter_item_mainhand_charges%</code></p>\n<h4>MythicMobs native (<code>&lt;counter...&gt;</code>)</h4>\n<p>Works directly inside skill lines and config strings — no PlaceholderAPI required. The subject is whichever entity (caster/target) is active where the placeholder is used.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;counter.KEY&gt;</code></td><td>Player-scoped counter on the context entity</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;counter.item.KEY&gt;</code></td><td>Item-scoped counter, mainhand item</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;counter.item.SLOT.KEY&gt;</code></td><td>Item-scoped counter on a specific equipment slot</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Slots: <code>mainhand</code>/<code>hand</code>, <code>offhand</code>, <code>head</code>/<code>helm</code>/<code>helmet</code>, <code>chest</code>/<code>chestplate</code>, <code>legs</code>/<code>leggings</code>, <code>feet</code>/<code>boots</code>.</p>\n<p>Returns <code>0</code> under the same absent/expired/wrong-entity-type/empty-slot conditions as the PlaceholderAPI form.</p>\n<p>Examples: <code>&lt;counter.soulkills&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;counter.item.charges&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;counter.item.offhand.charges&gt;</code></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Show remaining charges in a message when the wand is used\ncharged_wand_feedback:\n  Skills:\n    - message{m=&quot;&lt;charges: &lt;counter.item.charges&gt;&quot;} @self ~onUse</code></pre>\n<h3>Storage Format</h3>\n<p>Not usually something you need to know, but useful if you&#x27;re inspecting an item/player&#x27;s data directly (e.g. via <code>/data get</code>): each counter <code>&lt;key&gt;</code> is stored under the <code>mythicenchants</code> namespace as <code>counter_&lt;sanitized-key&gt;</code> (the value) plus <code>counter_&lt;sanitized-key&gt;_expiry</code> (only present if an expiry was ever set).</p>"},"enchants:mechanics/curezombievillager":{"h":"<hr>\n<p>title: CureZombieVillager</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>CureZombieVillager</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Cures a targeted Zombie Villager into a Villager.</p>\n<p>This mechanic supports either an instant conversion, where the Zombie Villager is immediately replaced with a Villager, or a vanilla-style conversion that preserves the Zombie Villager’s trades.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>How the Zombie Villager should be cured</td><td><code>INSTANT</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>INSTANT</code></td><td>Spawns a Villager at the Zombie Villager&#x27;s location, then removes the Zombie Villager.</td></tr><tr><td><code>VANILLA</code></td><td>Starts a vanilla Zombie Villager conversion with full trade preservation. The caster must be a player for this mode.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>CureZombieVillager:\n  Skills:\n  - curezombievillager{mode=vanilla} @target ~onRightClick\n  - curezombievillager{mode=instant;delay=60} @target ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>curezombievillager</code></li><li><code>cure</code></li><li><code>curezone</code></li><li><code>curevillager</code></li><li><code>cureinfected</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/curseitem":{"h":"<h2>Curse Item</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Applies or removes persistent curse markers (Binding or Vanishing) on the current item. Curse enforcement is handled by MythicEnchants listeners — Binding prevents unequipping, and Vanishing destroys the item on death.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>type</code></td><td><code>t</code></td><td>The curse type: <code>BINDING</code> or <code>VANISHING</code></td><td><code>BINDING</code></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>Whether to apply or remove the curse</td><td><code>APPLY</code></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The item slot to evaluate instead of the casting item</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>APPLY</code></td><td>Marks the item with the specified curse</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Removes the curse marker from the item</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>CurseOfBinding:\n  Skills:\n  - curseitem{type=BINDING;mode=APPLY} @self ~onEnchantApply\n  - curseitem{type=BINDING;mode=REMOVE} @self ~onEnchantRemove\n\nCurseOfVanishing:\n  Skills:\n  - curseitem{type=VANISHING;mode=APPLY} @self ~onEnchantApply\n  - curseitem{type=VANISHING;mode=REMOVE} @self ~onEnchantRemove</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>markcurse</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/enchant":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Add/Remove enchantments or enchant levels from an item.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>enchant</code>, <code>enchantment</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The Enchantment ID to modify</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code>, <code>function</code>, <code>f</code></td><td>The way the mechanic is adjustment the enchantment&#x27;s level</td><td><code>SET</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The enchantment level(s) used for mode adjustment</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The item slot to evaluate instead of the casting item</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>SET</code></td><td>Sets the enchantment on that item to the specified <code>level</code>, overwriting any levels of that enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADD</code></td><td>Adds the <code>level</code> amount to the item&#x27;s current enchantment level</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Removes the <code>level</code> amount from the item&#x27;s current enchantment level</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>Enchantment levels are capped at their configured maximum level, regardless of SET or ADD operations.\\ Enchantment levels being set or reduced to 0 or below will remove the enchantment from the item entirely.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>LunarUpgrade:\n  Skills:\n  # When this skill is activated, the triggering player&#x27;s helmet will increase its Lunar Light enchantment level by 1.\n  # If the helmet did not have the enchantment, it would gain it at level 1.\n  - enchant{id=LUNAR_LIGHT;l=1;slot=HELMET} @trigger</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>enchantitem</code></li><li><code>enchantment</code></li><li><code>mythicEnchant</code></li><li><code>meenchant</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/enchantattribute":{"h":"<h2>Enchant Attribute</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Applies or removes a persistent attribute modifier tied to the active enchant item on the entity. The modifier is keyed to the specific enchantment instance so equipping/unequipping correctly manages the modifier lifecycle.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>attribute</code></td><td><code>attr</code></td><td>The Bukkit attribute name or key (e.g. <code>SNEAKING_SPEED</code>, <code>MINING_EFFICIENCY</code>, <code>minecraft:oxygen_bonus</code>)</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>operation</code></td><td><code>op</code></td><td>The attribute operation: <code>ADD_NUMBER</code>, <code>ADD_SCALAR</code>, or <code>MULTIPLY_SCALAR_1</code></td><td><code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>The modifier amount</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>Whether to apply or remove the modifier</td><td><code>APPLY</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code></td><td>Optional custom modifier key suffix for multiple modifiers on the same attribute</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>APPLY</code></td><td>Applies the attribute modifier to the entity</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Removes the attribute modifier from the entity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>SwiftSneak:\n  Skills:\n  - enchantattribute{attribute=SNEAKING_SPEED;a=&lt;math:enchant_level*0.15&gt;;mode=APPLY} @self ~onEquip\n  - enchantattribute{attribute=SNEAKING_SPEED;mode=REMOVE} @self ~onUnequip</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>vanillaattribute</code></li><li><code>equipattribute</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/enchanttable":{"h":"<h2>Enchant Table</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Opens the MythicEnchants enchanting table for a player, optionally spoofing the bookshelf/power count so the table&#x27;s offers and level hints behave as if that many shelves surrounded it — with no real block edits. The spoofed value flows through the normal offer pipeline, so both the math and the visible level hints reflect it.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>power</code></td><td><code>bookshelves</code>, <code>shelves</code>, <code>p</code></td><td>Fake table power. When set, offers are computed from this value instead of a real block scan. Omit to use the normal scan at the player&#x27;s location.</td><td><i>real scan</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>force</code></td><td><code>f</code></td><td>Passed to <code>openEnchanting(loc, force)</code>. When <code>true</code>, the table opens even if the player isn&#x27;t standing at a real enchanting table</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>The override is per-player and is cleared automatically when the enchanting inventory closes, so it cannot leak into a later real table session.</li><li><code>power</code> is fed into the configured <code>table-power</code> slot equations as the <code>count</code> variable, exactly like a real scan — per-slot caps and <code>max-base-level</code> still apply.</li><li>Targets a player (caster via <code>@self</code>, or any player entity via a targeter). Non-players fail with <code>INVALID_TARGET</code>.</li></ul>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>ArcaneScholar:\n  Skills:\n  - enchanttable{power=15} @self ~onUse\n  - enchanttable{bookshelves=8;force=false} @target ~onInteract\n  - opentable{} @self ~onSneak</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>enchanttable</code></li><li><code>opentable</code></li><li><code>enchantingtable</code></li><li><code>openenchanting</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/enchseed":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Rerolls the enchanting seed on a player, resulting in new enchantment table offers.  This requires the <code>custom-table: true</code> setting in <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"info/config\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/info/config\">the plugin config</a> enabled for its enchantment handling.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>none</code></td><td><code>N/A</code></td><td>This mechanic has no attributes.</td><td>N/A</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>insight_wizard:\n  Type: VILLAGER\n  Skills:\n  - enchseed @trigger ~onInteract\n  - message{m=&quot; Wizard of Insight &gt; Ah yes, I shall enlighten you with new potential!&quot;} @trigger ~onInteract</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li>This mechanic has no aliases.</li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/experience":{"h":"<h2>Experience</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Modifies a player&#x27;s experience levels or points with point-accurate math, so removing points correctly rolls down into the previous level&#x27;s bar instead of clamping at the current level.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>How the mechanic adjusts the experience</td><td><code>ADD</code></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>unit</code></span></td><td><code>u</code></td><td>Whether <code>amount</code> is measured in points or levels</td><td><code>POINTS</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amnt</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>The integer amount to apply</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADD</code></td><td>Adds the amount to the player&#x27;s current experience</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Subtracts the amount (clamped at 0)</td></tr><tr><td><code>SET</code></td><td>Sets the experience to exactly the amount</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Units</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POINTS</code></td><td><code>POINT</code></td><td>Operates in absolute total XP points. Conversions use the real vanilla XP curve, so <code>REMOVE</code> rolls a player down into the previous level&#x27;s bar (e.g. 30 points = lvl 3 with 3/13 bar; <code>REMOVE 5</code> → 25 points = lvl 2 with 9/11 bar, not lvl 3 with an empty bar)</td></tr><tr><td><code>LEVELS</code></td><td><code>LEVEL</code></td><td>Operates on whole levels, preserving the current bar progress</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Greed:\n  Skills:\n  - experience{mode=ADD;unit=points;amount=&lt;math:enchant_level*5&gt;} @self ~onKill\n  - experience{m=REMOVE;u=points;a=5} @self ~onDamaged\n  - experience{m=SET;u=levels;a=10} @trigger ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>experience</code></li><li><code>xp</code></li><li><code>exp</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/fakedrops":{"h":"<h2>FakeDrops</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Spawns a decoy item entity at the break/death location that visually appears as one material (<code>initial</code>) but transforms into the real reward (<code>transform</code>) after a configurable delay. Supports Fortune-aware block drops, mob Looting drops, MythicMobs loot tables, and flat material rewards. An optional particle loop plays on the decoy while it waits.</p>\n<p>Works on both <code>~onBlockBreak</code> and <code>~onKill</code> triggers.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>initial</code></td><td><code>i</code></td><td>The decoy material displayed while the item waits</td><td><i>(required)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>transform</code></td><td><code>t</code></td><td>What the item becomes on reveal: a material name, a MythicMobs loot table name, or empty if using <code>fortune</code>/<code>looting</code></td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>d</code></td><td><code>revealdelay</code>, <code>smeltdelay</code>, <code>duration</code></td><td>Ticks before the item transforms. <b>Do not use <code>delay=</code></b> — that key is reserved by MythicMobs&#x27; base <code>SkillMechanic</code> as a whole-skill execution delay applied via MM&#x27;s own scheduler; using it here defers the <i>entire mechanic call</i> by N ticks instead of just the reveal, which breaks the synchronous <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> context (<code>cast()</code> sees a null block-break event)</td><td><code>20</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>pickup</code></td><td><code>p</code></td><td>Whether the decoy can be picked up before it transforms</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>fortune</code></td><td><code>f</code></td><td>Compute real drops with Fortune from the broken block and remap <code>initial</code> → <code>transform</code> on reveal</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>looting</code></td><td><code>l</code></td><td>On kill, regenerate the victim&#x27;s loot table respecting the killer&#x27;s Looting level</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>fire</code></td><td><code>flame</code></td><td>Sets the decoy on fire for the duration of the delay</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>glow</code></td><td><code>g</code></td><td>Makes the decoy glow</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>a</code></td><td>Item count when using a flat material <code>transform</code> (not used with <code>fortune</code> or <code>looting</code>)</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>blocktypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>blocks</code></td><td>Comma-separated material list — only fires if the broken block matches. Injected automatically by TriggerManager for <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> lines via <code>bt=</code>; static lines can use a <code>?triggerBlockType</code> condition instead.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (all blocks)</td></tr><tr><td><code>perdrop</code></td><td><code>perdurability</code>, <code>pd</code></td><td>Damage the tool by 1 durability per revealed drop item spawned</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>chanceperdrop</code></td><td><code>chance</code>, <code>dc</code></td><td>0–1 probability per spawned drop to consume 1 durability. Overrides <code>perdrop</code> when set (≥ 0).</td><td><code>-1</code> (disabled)</td></tr><tr><td><code>respectunbreaking</code></td><td><code>unbreaking</code>, <code>ru</code></td><td>Apply the vanilla Unbreaking negation roll before consuming durability</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Particle Attributes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>particle</code></td><td><code>par</code></td><td>Bukkit particle name to loop on the decoy (e.g. <code>DUST</code>, <code>FLAME</code>, <code>ENCHANT</code>)</td><td><i>(none)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>particlecolor</code></td><td><code>pc</code></td><td>Color for <code>DUST</code> particles — named color or <code>R,G,B</code></td><td><code>WHITE</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>particlesize</code></td><td><code>ps</code></td><td>Dust particle size</td><td><code>1.0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>particlecount</code></td><td><code>pn</code></td><td>Particles spawned per rate tick</td><td><code>3</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>particlespread</code></td><td><code>psp</code></td><td>Spread radius of each particle burst</td><td><code>0.15</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>particlerate</code></td><td><code>pr</code></td><td>Ticks between each particle burst</td><td><code>4</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Transform Resolution Order</h3>\n<p>When <code>reveal</code> fires, the mechanic resolves what to drop in this order:</p>\n<ol><li><b>Fortune</b> (<code>fortune=true</code>, block-break only) — uses the block&#x27;s natural drops computed at cast time. All stacks of <code>initial</code> material are replaced with <code>transform</code> material; other drops pass through unchanged.</li><li><b>Looting</b> (<code>looting=true</code>, kill only) — regenerates the victim&#x27;s loot table with the killer&#x27;s Looting modifier applied.</li><li><b>MythicMobs loot table</b> — if <code>transform</code> matches a known MM drop table name, generates from it.</li><li><b>Flat material</b> — spawns <code>amount</code> of the material named in <code>transform</code>.</li></ol>\n<h3>Custom Blocks</h3>\n<p>When the broken block is a Nexo, MythicCrucible, ItemsAdder, or CraftEngine custom block (see blockdrops the section for custom-blocks for what that means), <code>fortune=true</code> pulls &quot;natural drops&quot; from that addon&#x27;s own configured loot instead of <code>block.getDrops(tool)</code>:</p>\n<ul><li><b>Nexo</b> / <b>ItemsAdder</b> — the block&#x27;s real configured drop entries are read (<code>Drop.spawns(...)</code> / <code>CustomBlock.getLoot(tool, false)</code>), so the <code>initial</code>-material match works exactly as it does for a vanilla block.</li><li><b>CraftEngine</b> — the block&#x27;s own loot table is read via <code>ImmutableBlockState.getDrops(...)</code> with the held tool injected into context, same as <code>blockdrops</code>.</li><li><b>MythicCrucible</b> — its MythicMobs <code>DropTable</code> can&#x27;t be introspected for specific material membership (its internal drop entries don&#x27;t expose an item type generically), so any Crucible custom block with a non-empty drop table is treated as fortune-eligible unconditionally, and its real configured loot is what spawns on reveal — the <code>initial</code>/<code>transform</code> swap only affects the <i>decoy</i> item shown while waiting, not which materials from the table get replaced.</li></ul>\n<p><code>looting=true</code> is unaffected — it only applies on <code>~onKill</code> and never reads block state.</p>\n<p>Note: <code>blocktypes</code>/<code>bt</code> on this mechanic only matches plain vanilla materials (unlike <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>veinminer</code>, it has no <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> syntax) — to scope a <code>fortune=true</code> reveal to custom-block breaks specifically, use <code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> instead of a <code>blocktypes</code> filter (see the <code>disguised_custom_ore</code> example below).</p>\n<h3>Named Colors for <code>particlecolor</code></h3>\n<p><code>RED</code>, <code>GREEN</code>, <code>BLUE</code>, <code>WHITE</code>, <code>YELLOW</code>, <code>ORANGE</code>, <code>AQUA</code>, <code>PURPLE</code>, <code>FUCHSIA</code>, <code>GRAY</code>, <code>SILVER</code>, <code>LIME</code>, <code>MAROON</code>, <code>NAVY</code>, <code>OLIVE</code>, <code>TEAL</code>, <code>BLACK</code></p>\n<p>Or use <code>R,G,B</code> integer values: <code>particlecolor=255,128,0</code></p>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Disguise diamonds as coal — Fortune-aware, glowing, with dust particles\nauto_smelt:\n  Skills:\n    - fakedrops{i=COAL;transform=DIAMOND;d=40;fortune=true;glow=true;particle=DUST;pc=AQUA;bt=DIAMOND_ORE,DEEPSLATE_DIAMOND_ORE} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Spawn a MM loot table on kill after a delay\ncursed_loot:\n  Skills:\n    - fakedrops{i=BONE;transform=cursed_loot_table;d=60;fire=true} @self ~onKill\n\n# Simple material swap — iron drops gold after 1 second\ngilded_touch:\n  Skills:\n    - fakedrops{i=RAW_IRON;transform=GOLD_INGOT;d=20;amount=1;bt=IRON_ORE,DEEPSLATE_IRON_ORE} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Kill drop with Looting support and particles\nheadhunter:\n  Skills:\n    - fakedrops{i=BONE;transform=NETHER_STAR;d=30;looting=true;particle=ENCHANT;pn=5} @self ~onKill\n\n# Disguise a custom block&#x27;s real drop as coal until revealed (Nexo/Crucible/ItemsAdder/CraftEngine only)\ndisguised_custom_ore:\n  Skills:\n    - fakedrops{i=COAL;fortune=true;d=30;glow=true;particle=DUST;pc=PURPLE} @self ~onCustomBlockBreak</code></pre>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li><code>fortune=true</code> suppresses the block&#x27;s normal item drop at cast time (<code>setDropItems(false)</code>) and re-drops all non-<code>initial</code> items immediately. Only the <code>initial</code>-typed drops are held and remapped on reveal.</li><li><code>looting=true</code> does nothing on <code>~onBlockBreak</code>; <code>fortune=true</code> does nothing on <code>~onKill</code>.</li><li>If both <code>fortune</code> and <code>looting</code> are false and <code>transform</code> is empty, the mechanic logs a warning and returns without spawning any reveal drop.</li><li>The decoy entity is removed (not picked up) when reveal fires. If a player picks it up before reveal, the scheduler callback detects the entity is dead and exits silently.</li><li>Debug logging (all <code>[FakeDrops]</code> lines) is gated behind the plugin&#x27;s <code>debug: true</code> config flag.</li></ul>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>fakedrops</code></li><li><code>fakedrop</code></li><li><code>transformdrop</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/fireenchanttrigger":{"h":"<h2>Fire Enchant Trigger</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Fires the <code>onEnchantApply</code> or <code>onEnchantRemove</code> trigger on the caster&#x27;s held item. Useful for programmatically triggering enchantment lifecycle events from command skills or other mechanics.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>enchant</code>, <code>enchantment</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The enchantment ID to fire the trigger for. If empty, auto-detects changes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The enchantment level to report in the trigger</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>t</code></td><td>Which trigger event to fire</td><td><code>APPLY</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>source</code></td><td><code>src</code></td><td>The source identifier for the trigger event</td><td><code>SKILL</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>APPLY</code></td><td>Fires the <code>onEnchantApply</code> trigger</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Fires the <code>onEnchantRemove</code> trigger</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Manually fire apply trigger after enchanting via command\nForceApply:\n  Skills:\n  - fireenchanttrigger{id=SHARPNESS;l=3;mode=APPLY} @self\n\n# Fire remove trigger\nForceRemove:\n  Skills:\n  - fireenchanttrigger{id=SHARPNESS;mode=REMOVE} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>enchanttrigger</code></li><li><code>menchfire</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/fishingwaittime":{"h":"<h2>Fishing Wait Time</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Reduces the fishing hook&#x27;s minimum and maximum wait time by a flat tick amount. Supports a base reduction plus an additional reduction per enchantment level.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>base</code></td><td><code>b</code></td><td>Base tick reduction to apply to the wait time</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><code>per_level</code></td><td><code>perlevel</code>, <code>pl</code></td><td>Additional tick reduction per enchantment level</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Lure:\n  Skills:\n  - fishingwaittime{base=0;pl=100} @self ~onFish</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>fishingtime</code></li><li><code>luretime</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/frostwalker":{"h":"<h2>Frost Walker</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Freezes nearby surface water into frosted ice around the player. Supports configurable radius scaling per level and vanilla light-dependent melting or forced melt delays.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>Level override for radius calculation. If 0, derives from the current enchant level</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><code>baseradius</code></td><td><code>br</code></td><td>Base freeze radius in blocks</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><code>radiusperlevel</code></td><td><code>rpl</code></td><td>Additional radius per enchantment level</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><code>maxradius</code></td><td><code>mr</code></td><td>Maximum freeze radius cap</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td><code>vanilla</code></td><td><code>v</code></td><td>If true, uses vanilla light-dependent melting. If false, uses a fixed melt delay</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td><code>meltdelay</code></td><td><code>md</code>, <code>duration</code>, <code>d</code></td><td>Melt delay in ticks when <code>vanilla</code> is false</td><td>60</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>FrostWalker:\n  Skills:\n  - frostwalker{} @self ~onTimer:10\n\n# Custom frost walker with larger radius and slower melting\nDeepFreeze:\n  Skills:\n  - frostwalker{br=3;rpl=2;mr=20;vanilla=false;md=200} @self ~onTimer:10</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>freezewater</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/itemattribute":{"h":"<h2>Enchant Item Attribute</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Adds, modifies, or removes an AttributeModifier directly on the item&#x27;s metadata. Unlike <code>enchantattribute</code>, this persists on the item itself rather than on the entity, preserving tooltips and surviving across sessions.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>attribute</code></td><td><code>attr</code></td><td>The Bukkit attribute name or key (e.g. <code>ATTACK_DAMAGE</code>, <code>ARMOR</code>)</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>operation</code></td><td><code>op</code></td><td>The attribute operation: <code>ADD_NUMBER</code>, <code>ADD_SCALAR</code>, or <code>MULTIPLY_SCALAR_1</code></td><td><code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>The modifier amount</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>How the mechanic adjusts the attribute modifier</td><td><code>ADD</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code></td><td>Custom modifier key for identifying the modifier</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The item slot to evaluate instead of the casting item</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>equipslot</code></td><td><code>eslot</code>, <code>es</code></td><td>The equipment slot group the modifier applies to</td><td><code>any</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADD</code></td><td>Adds the amount to any existing modifier, or creates a new one</td></tr><tr><td><code>SET</code></td><td>Sets the modifier to the exact specified amount</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Removes the modifier from the item</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Sharpness:\n  Skills:\n  - itemattribute{attribute=ATTACK_DAMAGE;a=&lt;math:enchant_level*0.5&gt;;mode=SET;equipslot=MAINHAND} @self ~onEquip</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>itemattribute</code></li><li><code>itemattr</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/lootluck":{"h":"<h2>Loot Luck</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Stages loot-context luck and looting modifiers for the current loot event. The vanilla loot table is regenerated with the adjusted values, giving correct Fortune/Looting behavior.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>table</code></td><td><code>loottable</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>t</code></td><td>Explicit loot table key, or <code>AUTO</code> to detect from the event</td><td><code>AUTO</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>luck</code></td><td><code>l</code></td><td>Luck bonus to add to the loot context</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><code>looting</code></td><td><code>modifier</code>, <code>m</code></td><td>Looting modifier to apply to the loot context</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>For fishing luck (<code>minecraft:luck_of_the_sea</code>), the bundled vanilla override uses the datapack&#x27;s native <code>minecraft:fishing_luck_bonus</code> effect instead. Use <code>lootluck</code> only for custom fishing-luck enchants or mob kill looting.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Looting:\n  Skills:\n  - lootluck{looting=&lt;math:enchant_level&gt;} @trigger ~onKill\n\n# Custom fishing luck enchant\nFishingLuck:\n  Skills:\n  - lootluck{table=minecraft:gameplay/fishing;luck=&lt;math:enchant_level&gt;} @self ~onFishcatch</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>droploot</code></li><li><code>loottabledrop</code></li><li><code>bonusloot</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/loyalty":{"h":"<h2>Loyalty</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Sets the loyalty level on the currently thrown trident, causing it to return to the player after hitting a target or surface.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The loyalty level to set. If 0, derives from the current enchant level</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Loyalty:\n  Skills:\n  - loyalty{} @self ~onProjectile_throw</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>tridentloyalty</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/mechanics":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem mechanics MythicEnchants provides. These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Mechanics</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills.</p>\n<p>These registered mechanics may be used outside of enchantments as well, such as a mob granting an enchantment to a player&#x27;s item.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a> also grants item-related mechanics, such as durability changes!</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Combat Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/moddrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ModDrops\"><code>moddrops</code></a></td><td>Cancels original block or mob drops and replaces them with items from a MythicMobs drop table or a specific drop entry.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/reducedamage\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ReduceDamage\"><code>reducedamage</code></a></td><td>Reduces the current damage event by a flat amount.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/windburst\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/WindBurst\"><code>windburst</code></a></td><td>Launches the caster upward and knocks back nearby entities on a smash attack.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Datapack Mechanics</h3>\n<p>Some behaviors of enchantments are only handled through datapacks, which are only loaded during server startup. The following mechanic lines only work with the <code>~onDatapack</code> load trigger, and only configure the enchantment&#x27;s properties.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/channeling\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Channeling\"><code>channeling</code></a></td><td>The lightning-strike effect of thrown tridents.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/efficiency\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Efficiency\"><code>efficiency</code></a></td><td>The mining speed attribute bonus for tools.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/fishingluck\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/FishingLuck\"><code>fishingluck</code></a></td><td>The luck bonus for fishing loot tables.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/fishingtime\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/FishingTime\"><code>fishingtime</code></a></td><td>The fishing time reduction via datapack.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/infinity\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Infinity\"><code>infinity</code></a></td><td>The ammo use behavior for bows.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/lure\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Lure\"><code>lure</code></a></td><td>The fishing time reduction for fishing rods.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/protection\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Protection\"><code>protection</code></a></td><td>The damage reduction via datapack attributes.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/quickcharge\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/QuickCharge\"><code>quickcharge</code></a></td><td>The charge time reduction for crossbows.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/riptide\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Riptide\"><code>riptide</code></a></td><td>The propulsion effect of thrown tridents.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/sweepingedge\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/SweepingEdge\"><code>sweepingedge</code></a></td><td>The sweep damage ratio for swords.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Enchantment Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/curseitem\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/CurseItem\"><code>curseitem</code></a></td><td>Applies or removes persistent curse state on the current item.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/enchant\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Enchant\"><code>enchant</code></a></td><td>Adds, sets, or removes an enchantment level on a targeted entity&#x27;s item slot.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/enchantattribute\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/EnchantAttribute\"><code>enchantattribute</code></a></td><td>Applies or removes a persistent attribute modifier for the current enchant item.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/enchanttable\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/EnchantTable\"><code>enchanttable</code></a></td><td>Opens the MythicEnchants enchanting table for a player, optionally spoofing the bookshelf.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/enchseed\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/EnchSeed\"><code>enchseed</code></a></td><td>Rerolls the target player&#x27;s enchanting seed, changing their offered enchantments.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/experience\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Experience\"><code>experience</code></a></td><td>Modifies a player&#x27;s experience levels or points.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/fireenchanttrigger\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/FireEnchantTrigger\"><code>fireenchanttrigger</code></a></td><td>Fires the ENCHANT_APPLY or ENCHANT_REMOVE trigger on the caster&#x27;s held item.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/itemattribute\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ItemAttribute\"><code>itemattribute</code></a></td><td>Adds or removes an attribute modifier directly on the enchanted item.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/recoveritem\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/RecoverItem\"><code>recoveritem</code></a></td><td>Prevents the targeted item from being dropped on death, with optional limited uses.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Fishing Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/fishingwaittime\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/FishingWaitTime\"><code>fishingwaittime</code></a></td><td>Reduces fishing hook min/max wait time by a flat tick amount per enchantment level.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/lootluck\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/LootLuck\"><code>lootluck</code></a></td><td>Stages loot-context luck and looting modifiers for the current loot event.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Item &amp; Durability Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/blockdrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/BlockDrops\"><code>blockdrops</code></a></td><td>Drops the current block using the live held tool.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/fakedrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/FakeDrops\"><code>fakedrops</code></a></td><td>Spawns a decoy item entity at the break/death location.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/mendingrepair\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/MendingRepair\"><code>mendingrepair</code></a></td><td>Repairs the current trigger item using XP from the current gain event.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/reducedurability\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ReduceDurability\"><code>reducedurability</code></a></td><td>Damages the caster&#x27;s item durability by a flat amount or percentage.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/unbreaking\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Unbreaking\"><code>unbreaking</code></a></td><td>Rolls a per-point negate chance against the current item damage event.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/breakblockaction\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/BreakBlockAction\"><code>BreakBlockAction</code></a></td><td>Breaks the block at the target location.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Misc Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/curezombievillager\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/CureZombieVillager\"><code>curezombievillager</code></a></td><td>Allows the targeted Zombie Villager to be cured to a Villager.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/veinminer\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/VeinMiner\"><code>VeinMiner</code></a></td><td>Breaks all blocks within a configurable cube around the skill origin.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/counter\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Counter\"><code>Counter</code></a></td><td>A generic named counter for tracking arbitrary resources/stats — kill counts, soul shards, ability charges, streak.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Movement Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/frostwalker\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/FrostWalker\"><code>frostwalker</code></a></td><td>Freezes nearby surface water under the caster.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/soulspeed\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/SoulSpeed\"><code>soulspeed</code></a></td><td>Applies a movement speed attribute modifier while standing on configurable blocks.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Projectile Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/arrowbuff\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ArrowBuff\"><code>arrowbuff</code></a></td><td>Adds flat damage to the arrow projectile, scaling with critical hits.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/arrowfire\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ArrowFire\"><code>arrowfire</code></a></td><td>Sets the arrow projectile on fire for a duration in ticks.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/loyalty\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Loyalty\"><code>loyalty</code></a></td><td>Sets the loyalty level of the current thrown trident.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/piercing\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Piercing\"><code>piercing</code></a></td><td>Sets the pierce level of the current projectile.</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/projectilepath\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/ProjectilePath\"><code>projectilepath</code></a></td><td>Live ballistic aim-line preview while drawing a bow. <b>Use on <code>~onUse</code></b> — self-ticks until the player stops drawing.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Stat Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mechanic</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/playerstat\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/PlayerStat\"><code>playerstat</code></a></td><td>Adds or removes a MythicMobs stat modifier on the caster or target entity.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>LunarUpgrade:\n  Skills:\n  # When this skill is activated, the triggering player&#x27;s helmet will increase its Lunar Light enchantment level by 1.\n  # If the helmet did not have the enchantment, it would gain it at level 1.\n  - enchant{id=LUNAR_LIGHT;l=1;slot=HELMET} @trigger ~onInteract</code></pre>"},"enchants:mechanics/mendingrepair":{"h":"<h2>Mending Repair</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Repairs the trigger item using XP from the current experience gain event. The awarded XP is reduced proportionally to the amount of durability repaired, matching vanilla Mending behavior.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p><i>This mechanic has no configurable attributes.</i></p>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Mending:\n  Skills:\n  - mendingrepair{} @self ~onXp_gain</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>mending</code></li><li><code>repairwithxp</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/moddrops":{"h":"<h2>ModDrops</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Cancels the original drops from a block break or entity death and replaces them with items pulled from MythicMobs drop tables, specific drop entries, or both. Supports comma-separated lists to mix and match multiple tables and items in a single mechanic call.</p>\n<p>Works on both <code>~onBlockBreak</code> (block drops + XP) and <code>~onKill</code> (entity drops + XP, via <code>@target</code>).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>table</code></td><td><code>t</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of MythicMobs drop table names to roll</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>drop</code></td><td><code>d</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of drop entries — vanilla materials (<code>DIAMOND</code>), MythicMobs items, MythicCrucible items, or any registered MM drop type</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>quantity</code></td><td><code>q</code></td><td>How many times to pull each table/drop. Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code>.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>chance</code></td><td><code>c</code></td><td>Probability <code>[0.0–1.0]</code> that the replacement happens at all. If the roll fails, original drops are left untouched. Supports <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code>.</td><td><code>1.0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>block</code></td><td><code>b</code></td><td>Inline block-type filter (e.g. <code>STONE</code>) — only applies on <code>~onBlockBreak</code>. Convenience shortcut for a MythicMobs condition like <code>?blockType{t=STONE}</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (no filter)</td></tr><tr><td><code>entity</code></td><td><code>e</code></td><td>Inline entity-type filter (e.g. <code>ZOMBIE</code>) — only applies when the target is an entity.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (no filter)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>table</code> and <code>drop</code> can be combined — all tables are rolled first, then all drop entries are spawned.</p>\n<h3>Custom Blocks</h3>\n<p>Nexo, MythicCrucible, and ItemsAdder custom blocks (noteblock/mushroom/tripwire/chorus carriers, or ItemsAdder&#x27;s own block types — none with meaningful vanilla drops of their own) don&#x27;t need any special handling from this mechanic — <code>moddrops</code> never reads the broken block&#x27;s own drop table, only <code>table=</code>/<code>drop=</code>, so it&#x27;s addon-agnostic by construction. The only thing that matters is that vanilla drops and the addon&#x27;s own configured loot are both suppressed correctly, which happens upstream: <code>BlockInteractTrigger</code> (and <code>VeinMinerMechanic</code>, for vein-mined blocks) detect a custom block ahead of dispatch and only let that addon spawn its own loot if nothing downstream — including <code>moddrops</code> — calls <code>event.setDropItems(false)</code> first. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"blockdrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/blockdrops.md\">blockdrops.md</a> for the full mechanism.</p>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Replace stone drops with a custom drop table\nstone_enhanced:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{t=stone_enhanced} ~onBlockBreak ?blockType{t=STONE}\n\n# Same thing using the inline block filter\nstone_enhanced_inline:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{t=stone_enhanced;b=stone} ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Multiple tables at once\ndouble_loot:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{t=common_loot,rare_loot} @target ~onKill\n\n# Mix tables and specific items\nzombie_special:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{t=zombie_loot;d=ROTTEN_FLESH,SkeletonKingSword} @target ~onKill\n\n# Chance-based with enchant level scaling\nlucky_rot:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{drop=rotten_flesh;chance=(0.05*&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;)} @trigger ~onKill\n\n# Quantity scaling with enchant level\ndiamond_vein:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{d=DIAMOND;q=(2*&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;)} ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Multiple vanilla items\nbonus_kill:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{d=DIAMOND,EMERALD,GOLD_INGOT;c=0.5} @target ~onKill\n\n# Bonus MythicMobs drop table roll, custom blocks only (Nexo/Crucible/ItemsAdder)\ncustom_block_jackpot:\n  Skills:\n    - moddrops{t=jackpot_loot;chance=&lt;math:enchant_level*0.05&gt;} ~onCustomBlockBreak</code></pre>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>Block-break path: cancels <code>event.setDropItems(false)</code> and zeroes XP unconditionally (<code>event.setExpToDrop(0)</code>) before generating the replacement loot — unlike <code>blockdrops</code>, there&#x27;s no <code>exp=</code> toggle to keep vanilla XP.</li><li>Block-break path also snapshots attached-block physics drops (torches, rails, redstone dust, etc.) before suppressing, the same way <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>fakedrops</code> do — see <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"blockdrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/blockdrops.md\">blockdrops.md</a> for the full rationale. Skipped during a <code>veinminer</code> synthetic break to avoid double-dropping a neighbor already in that batch.</li><li>Entity-kill path doesn&#x27;t drop immediately — it stores the pending table/drop/quantity via <code>PendingModifyDropsStore</code>, keyed by the victim&#x27;s UUID, and the actual replacement happens when the death event resolves (so multiple <code>moddrops</code> casts on the same kill accumulate rather than racing).</li><li>If neither <code>table</code> nor <code>drop</code> resolves to anything (blank/invalid), the mechanic returns <code>INVALID_CONFIG</code> without touching drops.</li><li>The <code>block</code>/<code>entity</code> filters are a convenience shortcut only — equivalent MythicMobs conditions (<code>?blockType{...}</code>, entity-type conditions) work identically and can be combined with these filters.</li></ul>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>moddrops</code></li><li><code>modifydrops</code></li><li><code>changedrops</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/piercing":{"h":"<h2>Piercing</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Sets the pierce level of the projectile currently being fired. Allows arrows or other projectiles to pass through multiple entities.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The piercing level to set on the projectile. If 0, derives from the current enchant level</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Piercing:\n  Skills:\n  - piercing{} @self ~onShoot</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>projectilepiercing</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/playerstat":{"h":"<h2>Player Stat</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Adds or removes a MythicMobs stat modifier on the caster or target entity. This allows enchantments to interact with the MythicMobs stat system for custom stat scaling.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>stat</code></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The MythicMobs stat name to modify</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>val</code>, <code>v</code></td><td>The modifier amount</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"ilink\"><code>mode</code></span></td><td><code>m</code></td><td>Whether to add or remove the stat modifier</td><td><code>ADD</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>type</code></td><td><code>t</code>, <code>modifier</code>, <code>mod</code></td><td>The modifier type: <code>ADDITIVE</code>, <code>MULTIPLY_BASE</code>, or <code>MULTIPLY_TOTAL</code></td><td><code>ADDITIVE</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>src</code></td><td>Unique key for identifying this modifier</td><td><code>mench_default</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Modes</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADD</code></td><td>Adds the stat modifier to the entity</td></tr><tr><td><code>REMOVE</code></td><td>Removes the stat modifier from the entity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>CustomStrength:\n  Skills:\n  - playerstat{stat=STRENGTH;a=&lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;;mode=ADD;key=my_enchant} @self ~onEquip\n  - playerstat{stat=STRENGTH;mode=REMOVE;key=my_enchant} @self ~onUnequip</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>modifystat</code></li><li><code>statmodifier</code></li><li><code>menchstat</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/projectilepath":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Renders a live, ballistic trajectory preview while a player draws a bow, and optionally fires a skill at any living entity standing in the predicted path. Intended for the <code>~onUse</code> trigger: it fires once when the player starts drawing, then self-ticks (recalculating draw power, arc, and collision each tick) until the player releases, cancels, or switches away — so no <code>~onStopUse</code> line is needed. The path simulates real arrow physics (gravity + air drag) and stops at the first block or entity it would hit.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>particle</code></td><td><code>p</code></td><td>Particle type rendered along the path (any Bukkit <code>Particle</code> name).</td><td><code>CRIT</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>interval</code></td><td><code>i</code></td><td>Ticks between path redraws.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>step</code></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>Simulation step size (velocity multiplier per point). Smaller = denser/smoother line at higher cost.</td><td><code>1.0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>maxsteps</code></td><td><code>ms</code></td><td>Maximum simulation steps before the path stops (effective max range).</td><td><code>160</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>points</code></td><td><code>pts</code></td><td>Particles spawned at each path point.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>mindraw</code></td><td><code>md</code></td><td>Minimum bow-draw ticks before the path begins showing.</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>size</code></td><td><code>N/A</code></td><td>DUST particle size (only used when <code>particle=DUST</code>).</td><td><code>1.0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>color</code></td><td><code>c</code></td><td>DUST color as <code>R,G,B</code> (only used when <code>particle=DUST</code>).</td><td><code>255,255,255</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>onpathskill</code></td><td><code>ops</code>, <code>skill</code></td><td>Meta-skill cast when a living entity is detected in the path. Cast by the drawing player, targeted at the detected entity.</td><td><code>none</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>onpathcooldown</code></td><td><code>opcd</code></td><td>Ticks before the path-skill may fire again at the same target.</td><td><code>10</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>hunters_focus:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;7Hunter&#x27;&#x27;s Focus&#x27;\n  Description: Reveals your arrow&#x27;s flight path as you aim, and marks foes in your sights.\n  MaxLevel: 1\n  ValidSlots:\n  - MAINHAND\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/bow&#x27;\n  Skills:\n  - projectilepath{particle=DUST;color=255,40,40;size=1;mindraw=6;onpathskill=MarkTarget;opcd=20} @self ~onUse</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># The meta-skill referenced by onpathskill (place in your pack&#x27;s Skills file)\nMarkTarget:\n  Skills:\n  - potion{type=GLOWING;duration=40} @target\n  - effect:particles{p=villager_angry} @target</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>trajectory</code></li><li><code>aimline</code></li><li><code>predictpath</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/recoveritem":{"h":"<h2>Recover Item</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Prevents the targeted item from being dropped on death, implementing Soulbound-style item recovery. Supports limited uses tracked via persistent data containers, with options for deferred or immediate charge decrementing.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The item slot to recover</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td><code>uses</code>, <code>charges</code></td><td>Maximum number of recoveries. -1 for unlimited</td><td>-1</td></tr><tr><td><code>removepdc</code></td><td><code>rp</code>, <code>cleanpdc</code></td><td>Whether to remove the PDC tracking data after recovery</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td><code>reequip</code></td><td><code>req</code>, <code>equipslot</code></td><td>Whether to re-equip the item to its original slot after recovery</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td><code>uselevels</code></td><td><code>ul</code>, <code>leveluses</code>, <code>decrementlevel</code></td><td>Whether to decrement the enchantment level as a charge instead of a separate counter</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td><code>deferred</code></td><td><code>df</code>, <code>safedecrement</code>, <code>totemsafe</code></td><td>If true, defers charge decrementing to avoid conflicts with totem-of-undying and other death-cancelling mechanics</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Soulbound:\n  Skills:\n  - recoveritem{slot=TRIGGER;limit=3} @trigger ~onDeath\n\n# Unlimited soulbound with re-equip\nEternalBind:\n  Skills:\n  - recoveritem{reequip=true} @trigger ~onDeath\n\n# Level-based charges (level decreases each use)\nFragileSoul:\n  Skills:\n  - recoveritem{uselevels=true} @trigger ~onDeath</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>soulbound</code></li><li><code>itemrecover</code></li><li><code>keepitem</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/reducedamage":{"h":"<h2>Reduce Damage</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Reduces the current live damage event by a flat amount. Optionally filters by damage cause and reduces fire burn ticks. Intended for use with the <code>~onDamaged</code> trigger.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>The flat amount to subtract from incoming damage</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><code>burnreduction</code></td><td><code>burn</code>, <code>b</code></td><td>Amount to reduce fire burn ticks by</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td><code>cap</code></td><td><code>maxreduction</code>, <code>max</code></td><td>Maximum percentage of damage that can be reduced (0.0–1.0)</td><td>0.80</td></tr><tr><td><code>cause</code></td><td><code>causes</code>, <code>c</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of <code>EntityDamageEvent.DamageCause</code> values to filter by. If empty, applies to all causes</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Protection:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedamage{a=&lt;math:damage*0.08*enchant_level&gt;} @self ~onDamaged\n\nProjectileProtection:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedamage{a=&lt;math:damage*0.08*enchant_level&gt;;cause=PROJECTILE} @self ~onDamaged\n\nFireProtection:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedamage{a=&lt;math:damage*0.08*enchant_level&gt;;burn=&lt;math:enchant_level*15&gt;;cause=FIRE,FIRE_TICK,LAVA,HOT_FLOOR} @self ~onDamaged</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>protectdamage</code></li><li><code>vanillaprotection</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/reducedurability":{"h":"<h2>Reduce Durability</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Damages the caster&#x27;s item durability by a flat amount or percentage. Can optionally respect the Unbreaking enchantment&#x27;s negate chance.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>a</code></td><td>The durability damage amount (flat, or percentage if <code>percent</code> is true)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><code>percent</code></td><td><code>p</code></td><td>If true, <code>amount</code> is treated as a percentage of max durability (0.0–1.0)</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td><code>respectunbreaking</code></td><td><code>unbreaking</code>, <code>ru</code></td><td>Whether to apply unbreaking negate chance before damaging</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Frost Walker durability cost\nFrostWalker:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedurability{a=2} @self ~onTimer:10\n\n# Percentage-based durability cost\nHeavyStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - reducedurability{a=0.05;percent=true;unbreaking=false} @self ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>durabilityreduce</code></li><li><code>itemdamage</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/soulspeed":{"h":"<h2>Soul Speed</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Applies a movement speed attribute modifier while the caster stands on configurable block types. By default, emulates vanilla Soul Speed on Soul Sand and Soul Soil.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>amount</code></td><td><code>amt</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>The speed modifier amount</td><td>0.0405</td></tr><tr><td><code>operation</code></td><td><code>op</code>, <code>o</code></td><td>The attribute operation: <code>ADD_NUMBER</code>, <code>ADD_SCALAR</code>, or <code>MULTIPLY_SCALAR_1</code></td><td><code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>blocks</code></td><td><code>b</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of block material names to activate on</td><td><code>SOUL_SAND,SOUL_SOIL</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>SoulSpeed:\n  Skills:\n    - soulspeed{a=&lt;math.1.2379+0.1808*enchant_level&gt;;op=MULTIPLY;blocks=SOUL_SAND} @self ~onTimer:10\n# Custom speed boost on ice blocks\nIceRunner:\n  Skills:\n  - soulspeed{a=0.06;blocks=ICE,PACKED_ICE,BLUE_ICE} @self ~onTimer:10</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>soulspeedboost</code></li><li><code>blockspeedboost</code></li><li><code>blockspeed</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/unbreaking":{"h":"<h2>Unbreaking</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Applies vanilla-style unbreaking rolls to the live durability damage event. Each point of unbreaking level gives a chance to negate the durability loss entirely.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>chance</code></td><td><code>negatechance</code>, <code>c</code></td><td>Custom negate chance per level (0.0–1.0). If -1, uses vanilla formula</td><td>-1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>Unbreaking:\n  Skills:\n  - unbreaking{} @self ~onItem_damage</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>unbreakingitem</code></li><li><code>durabilityguard</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/veinminer":{"h":"<h2>VeinMiner</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Breaks all blocks within a configurable cube around the skill origin that match a block tag and/or material list. Each block fires a synthetic <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> so protection plugins can veto individual breaks. Drops respect Fortune and Silk Touch when <code>usetool=true</code>.</p>\n<p>Origin is set automatically by MythicEnchants on <code>~onBlockBreak</code> — point <code>@self</code> at the mechanic and it will center on the block that was broken.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>t</code></td><td><code>type</code>, <code>tag</code>, <code>types</code>, <code>blocks</code></td><td>Comma-separated list of block tags (<code>#minecraft:logs</code>), material names (<code>COAL_ORE</code>), and/or <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> custom-block ids. All can be mixed freely.</td><td><code>#minecraft:logs</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>rx</code></td><td><code>radiusx</code>, <code>r</code></td><td>Horizontal X radius in blocks</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>ry</code></td><td><code>radiusy</code></td><td>Vertical Y radius in blocks</td><td><code>24</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>rz</code></td><td><code>radiusz</code></td><td>Horizontal Z radius in blocks</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>drops</code></td><td><code>d</code></td><td>Whether to drop items from broken blocks</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>usetool</code></td><td><code>tool</code></td><td>Use the player&#x27;s held tool for drops, enabling Fortune and Silk Touch</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>maxblocks</code></td><td><code>max</code>, <code>mb</code></td><td>Maximum number of blocks to break per cast. <code>0</code> = unlimited.</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>perdrop</code></td><td><code>perdurability</code>, <code>pd</code></td><td>Damage the tool by 1 durability per block broken</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>chanceperdrop</code></td><td><code>chance</code>, <code>dc</code></td><td>0–1 probability per block to consume 1 durability. Overrides <code>perdrop</code> when set (≥ 0).</td><td><code>-1</code> (disabled)</td></tr><tr><td><code>respectunbreaking</code></td><td><code>unbreaking</code>, <code>ru</code></td><td>Apply the vanilla Unbreaking negation roll before consuming durability</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>perblock</code></td><td><code>perblockspertick</code>, <code>bpt</code></td><td>Blocks broken per tick, spreading a large vein across multiple ticks instead of one synchronous loop. <code>0</code> = instant/unthrottled (old behavior).</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>tickdelay</code></td><td><code>spreaddelay</code>, <code>spreadticks</code></td><td>Ticks to wait between each batch of <code>perblock</code> blocks. Only relevant when <code>perblock &gt; 0</code>.</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Block Matching</h3>\n<p>Each entry in <code>t</code> is resolved at load time:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Example</th><th>Resolves as</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>#namespace:tag</code></td><td><code>#minecraft:logs</code></td><td>Bukkit block tag — matches all tagged materials</td></tr><tr><td><code>#tag</code> (no namespace)</td><td><code>#logs</code></td><td>Shorthand — <code>minecraft:</code> namespace is assumed</td></tr><tr><td><code>MATERIAL</code></td><td><code>COAL_ORE</code></td><td>Exact Bukkit <code>Material</code> match</td></tr><tr><td><code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>nexo:ruby_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific Nexo custom block by its item id</td></tr><tr><td><code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>crucible:sapphire_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific MythicCrucible custom block by its internal item id</td></tr><tr><td><code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>itemsadder:topaz_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific ItemsAdder custom block by its namespaced id</td></tr><tr><td><code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>craftengine:emerald_ore</code></td><td>Matches a specific CraftEngine custom block by its namespaced id</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Unknown tags and materials log a warning at startup and are silently skipped at runtime.</p>\n<h3>Custom Blocks</h3>\n<p>Nexo/MythicCrucible/ItemsAdder/CraftEngine custom blocks matched by <code>t=</code> are broken <b>without ever publishing a real <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> for that addon to see</b> — its own break handling (which would otherwise spawn its configured loot directly, unsuppressably, before any enchant mechanic gets a chance to react) never runs for vein-mined custom blocks. Instead, <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> are dispatched directly in-process for each one, and <code>blockdrops</code>/this mechanic&#x27;s own fallback produce the drops — same output as breaking one manually. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"blockdrops\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/blockdrops.md\">blockdrops.md#custom-blocks</a> for the full mechanism this builds on.</p>\n<p>Note: <code>?triggerBlockType</code>/<code>?blockType</code> conditions only understand vanilla <code>Material</code> names via MythicMobs&#x27; own built-in parser — they can&#x27;t be given <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>craftengine:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries the way <code>veinminer{t=...}</code>&#x27;s own filter can, so scoping a vein-mine enchant to &quot;only ores, including a custom one&quot; has to happen via <code>t=</code> on the mechanic itself, not a condition.</p>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Timber enchant — fell a whole tree when a log is broken\ntimber:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:logs;rx=2;ry=24;rz=2} @self ~onBlockBreak ?triggerBlockType{t=#minecraft:logs}\n    - sound{s=entity.player.attack.sweep;v=0.7;p=0.8} @self ~onBlockBreak ?triggerBlockType{t=#minecraft:logs}\n\n# Vein miner enchant — break connected ore veins\nvein_miner:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:coal_ores,#minecraft:iron_ores,#minecraft:gold_ores;rx=3;ry=3;rz=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Mixed tag + material\nmushroom_feller:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:logs,MUSHROOM_STEM,BROWN_MUSHROOM_BLOCK,RED_MUSHROOM_BLOCK;rx=2;ry=24;rz=2} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Vein-mine custom ores from all four addons alongside vanilla ones\ncustom_vein_miner:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:coal_ores,nexo:ruby_ore,crucible:sapphire_ore,itemsadder:topaz_ore,craftengine:emerald_ore;rx=3;ry=3;rz=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n\n# Same vein-miner, plus extra drops on just the custom-block portion of the vein\ncustom_vein_miner_bonus:\n  Skills:\n    - veinminer{t=#minecraft:coal_ores,nexo:ruby_ore;rx=3;ry=3;rz=3} @self ~onBlockBreak\n    - blockdrops{mult=2} @self ~onCustomBlockBreak</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>veinminer</code></li><li><code>vein</code></li><li><code>fellblocks</code></li></ul>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>The mechanic is <code>INoTargetSkill</code> — it reads the skill origin directly and does not use location targets. Always pair it with <code>@self</code>; <code>@origin</code> or <code>@triggerlocation</code> will have no effect on which blocks it breaks.</li><li>The center block (the one the player actually struck) is never included in the break set — it was already broken and already dispatched <code>~onBlockBreak</code> by the real event that fired this skill. Only the surrounding matched blocks are this mechanic&#x27;s to break.</li><li>Each block it breaks (other than the center) fires a real <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code> dispatch, so other enchants on the tool (Fortune-style <code>blockdrops</code>, <code>fakedrops</code>, etc.) react per-block exactly as if the player had broken each one manually. Because <code>veinminer{}</code> is typically on that same trigger, this dispatch re-fires <code>veinminer{}</code> itself for every block it breaks — a dedicated re-entrancy guard makes any such nested/self-triggered invocation a no-op (it does not break a second cube centered on that block), so only the original player-initiated break ever starts a vein-mine.</li><li>With <code>perblock &gt; 0</code> (default), breaking is spread across ticks — some blocks in the vein may still be standing for a moment after the cast returns. A following skill line on the same <code>~onBlockBreak</code> trigger that depends on the whole vein already being gone should set <code>perblock=0</code> to force the old fully-synchronous behavior.</li><li>Setting <code>drops=false</code> removes blocks with <code>setType(AIR)</code> without any drops or sounds.</li></ul>"},"enchants:mechanics/windburst":{"h":"<h2>Wind Burst</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Emulates the vanilla Wind Burst mace enchantment. Launches the caster upward and knocks back nearby entities on a smash attack. By default, requires the caster to be falling.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>launchbase</code></td><td><code>lb</code></td><td>Base upward launch velocity</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td><code>launchperlevel</code></td><td><code>lpl</code></td><td>Additional launch velocity per enchantment level</td><td>0.5</td></tr><tr><td><code>knockbackradius</code></td><td><code>kr</code></td><td>Radius around the impact point to knock back entities</td><td>3.5</td></tr><tr><td><code>knockbackstrength</code></td><td><code>ks</code></td><td>Knockback strength applied to nearby entities</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td><code>requirefalling</code></td><td><code>rf</code></td><td>Whether the caster must be falling for the mechanic to activate</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td><code>particles</code></td><td><code>p</code></td><td>Whether to display wind burst particles</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td><code>sound</code></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>Whether to play the wind burst sound effect</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>WindBurst:\n  Skills:\n  - windburst{} @self ~onAttack\n\n# Custom wind burst with larger knockback\nHeavyImpact:\n  Skills:\n  - windburst{lb=1.0;lpl=0.75;kr=5.0;ks=2.0} @self ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>windcharge</code></li><li><code>windburstmace</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:targeters/enchantmentitem":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Targets the item casting the enchantment skill.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.\\ If using <a href=\"https://mythiccraft.io/index.php?resources/crucible-custom-items-armor-furniture-blocks-more.2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this targeter within skills triggered by MythicCrucible item skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>none</code></td><td></td><td>This targeter has no attributes currently.</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>specialItemUse:\n  Skills:\n  # This meta-skill&#x27;s original target receives an info message\n  - message{msg=&quot;The item magically repaired itself!&quot;}\n  # But the item that cast the skill receives the durability repair\n  - durability{a=20} @item</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>castingItem</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:targeters/targeters":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem targeters MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Targeters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Targeters</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills.</p>\n<h3>Enchantment Targeters</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Targeter</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"targeters/enchantmentitem\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Targeters/enchantmentItem\"><code>@enchantmentItem</code></a></td><td>The item casting the enchantment skill</td></tr><tr><td><code>@shotProjectile</code></td><td>Returns the <b>projectile entity</b> of the in-flight shoot/launch/hit event</td></tr><tr><td><code>@projectileOrigin</code></td><td>Returns the projectile&#x27;s <b>launch location</b> (spawn/muzzle point; on a hit event, the impact point)</td></tr><tr><td><code>@projectileDestination</code></td><td>Returns the projectile&#x27;s <b>destination location</b> — on impact, the hit point; on shoot/launch, a ray-trace forward along velocity (up to 64 blocks)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>"},"enchants:conditions/batchedchance":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>A chance that is rolled <b>once</b> and shared across multiple skill lines, so effects on different triggers (and different ticks) fire together — or not at all — on the same probability. A normal per-line <code>[chance]</code> rolls independently on every line, so two different-time events can never be linked to one decision; this condition fixes that. The roll is cached per <b>caster + key</b> and reused until it has been read <code>consume</code> times, then it resets so the next round re-rolls.</p>\n<h3>Auto-keying (zero config)</h3>\n<p>The <code>key</code> is optional. When omitted, it is derived automatically from the <b>firing enchantment&#x27;s ID</b>, so every no-key <code>batchedchance</code> line on the same enchant shares one roll — the enchant procs as a whole or not at all, with no key to type. Provide an explicit <code>key</code> only when one enchant needs several independent batches, or when used outside a MythicEnchants enchant (no enchant context available — falls back to a shared <code>auto</code> key).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>key</code></td><td><code>k</code>, <code>id</code></td><td>Identifier linking the lines that share one roll.</td><td><i>auto: firing enchant ID</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>chance</code></td><td><code>c</code></td><td>Probability <code>0.0</code>–<code>1.0</code> used on the first (deciding) check.</td><td><code>0.5</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>consume</code></td><td><code>uses</code>, <code>n</code></td><td>How many checks share the cached roll before it resets. Set to the number of lines sharing the key.</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Zero-config: both lines auto-link by enchant ID, sharing one 20% roll.\nfrost_combo:\n  Skills:\n  - skill{s=FrostStrike} @target ?batchedchance{chance=0.2} ~onAttack\n  - skill{s=FrostShot}   @self   ?batchedchance{chance=0.2} ~onShoot</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Explicit keys: two independent batches on one enchant.\nstorm_brand:\n  Skills:\n  - skill{s=A} @target ?batchedchance{chance=0.2;key=combo1} ~onAttack\n  - skill{s=B} @self   ?batchedchance{chance=0.2;key=combo1} ~onShoot\n  - skill{s=C} @target ?batchedchance{chance=0.5;key=combo2;consume=2} ~onDamaged</code></pre>\n<h3>Notes</h3>\n<ul><li>The <code>chance</code> is decided on the <b>first</b> check; lines sharing a roll should use the same <code>chance</code> (later differing values are ignored until the roll resets).</li><li>Set <code>consume</code> to the number of lines that share the key (default <code>2</code> = a pair). If a paired event sometimes never fires, the cached roll lingers until its <code>consume</code> count is reached.</li><li>The roll is <b>per caster</b>, so players never share each other&#x27;s rolls.</li></ul>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>linkedchance</code></li><li><code>sharedchance</code></li><li><code>batchchance</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/conditions":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem conditions MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Conditions</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills, including in-line condition evaluations.</p>\n<p>These registered conditions may be used outside of enchantments as well, such as a mob&#x27;s skills evaluating a player&#x27;s item for enchantments or durability.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a> also grants item-related conditions, such as checking an item&#x27;s model.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchanted Item Conditions</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/mench\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/mench\"><code>hasMythicEnchant</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the item has a specific enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/itemdurability\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemDurability\"><code>itemDurability</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the remaining durability available on the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/itemuseddurability\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemUsedDurability\"><code>itemUsedDurability</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the amount of lost durability on the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/itemdurabilitypercent\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/itemDurabilityPercent\"><code>itemDurabilityPercent</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the remaining durability percentage on the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/soulbounduses\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/soulbounduses\"><code>soulbounduses</code></a></td><td>Evaluates the remaining <code>recoveritem</code> uses/charges on the trigger item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/batchedchance\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/BatchedChance\"><code>batchedchance</code></a></td><td>A chance that is rolled <b>once</b> and shared across multiple skill lines</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/lethalcheck\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/lethalcheck\"><code>lethalcheck</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the current damage event would kill the target entity</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/customblock\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/customblock\"><code>customblock</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the current block-break&#x27;s block is a custom block</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/custombir\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/custombir\"><code>custombir</code></a></td><td>Checks whether Nexo, MythicCrucible, and/or ItemsAdder custom blocks are present within enchanting-table range</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Player Conditions</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"conditions/hasexperience\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Conditions/HasExperience\"><code>hasExperience</code></a></td><td>Evaluates whether the player has a range of exp points or levels</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Skills:\n  # Extra damage to undead mobs\n  - damage{amount=2*&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;} @target ~onAttack ?entitytype{type=ZOMBIE,SKELETON}\n  - potion{p=WEAKNESS;d=100;l=&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;} @target ~onAttack ?entitytype{type=HUSK} ?!mmType{t=SuperHusk,HuskFriend}</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>\n  # The item repairs itself when hitting metal enemies, using the MythicCrucible item-skill mechanic for durability.\n  - readucedurability{a=-3} @self ~onAttack ?entitytype{type=IRON_GOLEM} ?itemUsedDurability{damage=&gt;0}</code></pre>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  # Requires 50+ levels to gain bonus drops. \n  - dropitem{i=DIAMOND} @triggerlocation ~onKill ?hasExperience{unit=LEVELS;amount=&gt;50}</code></pre>"},"enchants:conditions/custombir":{"h":"<h2>Custom Block In Range</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks whether Nexo, MythicCrucible, and/or ItemsAdder custom blocks are present within enchanting-table range, using the same scan pattern uses (vanilla&#x27;s 30-cell bookshelf layout, or a chebyshev-cuboid radius). Intended for the <code>Enchanting.Conditions</code> block of an enchantment definition — it evaluates against the enchanting table&#x27;s block location, not the caster.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Addon</code></td><td><code>a</code>, <code>source</code></td><td>Restrict matching to one addon</td><td><i>(any addon)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>BlockTypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>ids</code></td><td>Comma-separated <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code> / <code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code> / <code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries. Each entry is checked independently against <code>Count</code> — <code>Require=all</code> means every listed id must independently reach <code>Count</code> somewhere in range, not that a single block matches all of them</td><td><i>(any custom block)</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>Require</code></td><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>all</code> — every <code>BlockTypes</code> entry must reach <code>Count</code>; <code>any</code> — at least one must. Ignored when <code>BlockTypes</code> is empty</td><td><code>all</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Count</code></td><td><code>c</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>amount</code></td><td>Minimum number of matching blocks required. Values below 1 are treated as 1</td><td><code>1</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Radius</code></td><td><code>r</code></td><td>Chebyshev radius (XZ) of the scan. <code>0</code> uses the vanilla 30-cell bookshelf pattern instead of a cuboid</td><td><code>0</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Los</code></td><td><code>lineofsight</code></td><td>Whether an air gap is required between the table and each candidate block (vanilla&#x27;s line-of-sight rule)</td><td><code>true</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Addon</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Nexo</code></td><td></td><td>Only Nexo custom blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>Crucible</code></td><td><code>MythicCrucible</code></td><td>Only MythicCrucible custom blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>ItemsAdder</code></td><td></td><td>Only ItemsAdder custom blocks</td></tr><tr><td><i>(empty)</i></td><td></td><td>Any of the three addons</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># A specific Crucible ore must be nearby, scanning a 3-block cuboid radius\ncustom_ore_sense:\n  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n    - custombir{bt=crucible:sapphire_ore;radius=3}\n\n# Requires at least 3 of a specific Nexo ore nearby (not just one)\ndeep_vein_bonus:\n  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n    - custombir{bt=nexo:ruby_ore;count=3}\n\n# Either of two Nexo blocks satisfies it, and only ItemsAdder blocks count otherwise\nmixed_source:\n  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n    - custombir{bt=nexo:ruby_ore,nexo:sapphire_ore;require=any}\n    - custombir{addon=itemsadder}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>custombir</code></li><li><code>cbr</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/customblock":{"h":"<h4><code>?customblock</code> Condition</h4>\n<p>A standalone MythicMobs condition (aliases: <code>?custblock</code>, <code>?iscustomblock</code>) for gating <i>any</i> mechanic — not just the drop mechanics above — on whether the current block-break&#x27;s block is a custom block. Reads from the same <code>BlockBreakEvent</code> context as <code>blockdrops</code>/<code>veinminer</code>/etc., so it only evaluates meaningfully inside a <code>~onBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onCustomBlockBreak</code>/<code>~onStartdestroyblock</code> skill line.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>addon</code></td><td><code>a</code>, <code>source</code></td><td>Restrict to one addon: <code>nexo</code>, <code>crucible</code>, or <code>itemsadder</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (any addon)</td></tr><tr><td><code>blocktypes</code></td><td><code>bt</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>ids</code></td><td>Comma-separated <code>nexo:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>crucible:&lt;id&gt;</code>/<code>itemsadder:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries — matches a specific custom block by id, same syntax as <code>blockdrops{bt=...}</code>.</td><td><code>&quot;&quot;</code> (any custom block)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Any custom block, any addon\n- particle{p=totem;a=10} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock\n\n# Only Nexo custom blocks\n- sound{s=block.amethyst_block.chime} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock{addon=nexo}\n\n# A specific MythicCrucible ore\n- effect:message{m=&quot;&lt;gold&gt;You struck sapphire!&quot;} @self ~onBlockBreak ?customblock{bt=crucible:sapphire_ore}</code></pre>"},"enchants:conditions/hasexperience":{"h":"<hr>\n<p>title: HasExperience</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Has Enchantment</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks total XP orb points using the same accurate math as the <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"mechanics/experience\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Mechanics/Experience\">ExperienceMechanic</a>.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Unit</code></td><td><code>u</code></td><td>The Type of experience to check</td><td>POINTS</td></tr><tr><td><code>Amount</code></td><td><code>a</code>,</td><td>Range of experience to check</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Unit</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Points</code></td><td><code>Point</code></td><td>Operates in absolute total XP points. Conversions use the real vanilla XP curve, so <code>REMOVE</code> rolls a player down into the previous level&#x27;s bar (e.g. 30 points = lvl 3 with 3/13 bar; <code>REMOVE 5</code> → 25 points = lvl 2 with 9/11 bar, not lvl 3 with an empty bar)</td></tr><tr><td><code>Levels</code></td><td><code>Level</code></td><td>Operates on whole levels, preserving the current bar progress</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Steals experience points based on Enchantment Level\nswiper:\n  Cooldown: 3\n  TriggerConditions:\n  - isPlayer\n  - hasExperience{unit=POINTS;amount=&gt;&lt;math.enchant_level*10+5&gt;}\n  Skills:\n  - experience{mode=REMOVE;unit=POINTS;amount=&lt;math.enchant_level*10+5&gt;}\n  - experience{mode=ADD;unit=POINTS;amount=&lt;math.enchant_level*10+5&gt;} @self\n\n# Deals damage to players who have more than 30 exp levels\nswiper_damage:\n  TriggerConditions:\n  - isPlayer\n  - hasExperience{unit=LEVELS;amount=&gt;30}\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=10}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>hasxp</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/hasmythicenchant":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates if the target item/slot has a specific enchantment managed by MythicEnchants (which includes custom and vanilla enchantments unless otherwise configured).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>enchant</code>, <code>enchantment</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The Enchantment ID to look for</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>The enchantment level(s) to look for, accepts ranges</td><td>&gt;0</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The item slot to evaluate instead of the casting item</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>LunarEnchantCheck:\n  TriggerConditions:\n  - hasMythicEnchant{id=LUNAR_LIGHT;slot=HELMET} true # Checks if the triggering player is wearing helmet enchanted with Lunar Light of any level\n  - hasMythicEnchant{e=LUNAR_LEAPING;slot=LEGS;l=2to3} true # Checks if the trigger player is wearing leggings with the Lunar Leaping enchantment of at level 2 or 3\n  - hasEnch{enchant=SOLAR_SHIELD;s=CHEST} castInstead SolarEnchantDecline # Denies the skill if the triggering player is wearing a chestplate with the Solar Shield enchantment\n  Skills:\n  - message{m=&quot;You truly are blessed by the moon herself!&quot;} @trigger\nSolarEnchantDecline:\n  Skills:\n  - message{m=&quot;Your armor shines too brightly for the moonlight to assist you.&quot;} @trigger</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>MythicEnchants</code></li><li><code>hasMythicEnchantment</code></li><li><code>hasEnch</code>  [⚠️shorthand distinguishes this from Mythic&#x27;s vanilla-only condition <code>hasEnchant</code>]</li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/itemdurability":{"h":"<h2>Item Durability</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates the remaining durability available on the enchanted item. Returns the number of durability points left before the item breaks.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>v</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>Remaining durability to check against</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has durability)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Value Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact remaining durability</td><td><code>100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a durability range (inclusive)</td><td><code>50to100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N durability remaining</td><td><code>&gt;50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N durability remaining</td><td><code>&gt;=100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Fewer than N durability remaining</td><td><code>&lt;10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N durability remaining</td><td><code>&lt;=50</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Warn when item is about to break\nLowDurabilityWarning:\n  Skills:\n  - message{msg=&quot;&amp;cYour weapon is about to break!&quot;} @self ?itemdurability{value=&lt;10} ~onAttack\n\n# Bonus damage at full durability\nPristineStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;} @trigger ?itemdurability{value=&gt;=250;slot=HAND} ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>durability</code></li><li><code>remainingdurability</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/itemdurabilitypercent":{"h":"<h2>Item Durability Percent</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates the remaining durability percentage on the enchanted item. Returns a value from 0 to 100, where 100 means full durability and 0 means about to break.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>v</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>Remaining durability percentage to check against (0–100)</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has durability)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Value Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact percentage</td><td><code>50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a percentage range (inclusive)</td><td><code>25to75</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N% remaining</td><td><code>&gt;50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N% remaining</td><td><code>&gt;=25</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Less than N% remaining</td><td><code>&lt;10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N% remaining</td><td><code>&lt;=50</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Warn when below 10% durability\nCriticalDurability:\n  Skills:\n  - message{msg=&quot;&amp;4&amp;lItem critically damaged!&quot;} @self ?itemdurabilitypercent{value=&lt;10} ~onItem_damage\n\n# Bonus effect when item is above 90%\nWellMaintained:\n  Skills:\n  - potion{t=HASTE;d=40;l=1} @self ?itemdurabilitypercent{value=&gt;=90} ~onBlock_break\n\n# Desperate power when item is nearly broken\nLastStand:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*5&gt;} @trigger ?itemdurabilitypercent{value=&lt;25} ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>durabilitypercent</code></li><li><code>durabilitypercentage</code></li><li><code>durabilitypct</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/itemuseddurability":{"h":"<h2>Item Used Durability</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates the amount of lost durability on the enchanted item. Returns the number of durability points that have been consumed (damage dealt to the item).</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>value</code></td><td><code>v</code>, <code>amount</code>, <code>a</code></td><td>Used durability to check against</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has taken damage)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Value Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact used durability</td><td><code>50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a used durability range (inclusive)</td><td><code>10to50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N durability used</td><td><code>&gt;100</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N durability used</td><td><code>&gt;=50</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Fewer than N durability used</td><td><code>&lt;10</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N durability used</td><td><code>&lt;=25</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Power scales with wear\nBattleHardened:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*3&gt;} @trigger ?itemuseddurability{value=&gt;=100} ~onAttack\n\n# Only trigger on pristine items (no durability used)\nMintCondition:\n  Skills:\n  - particles{p=happy_villager} @self ?itemuseddurability{value=0} ~onEquip</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>useddurability</code></li><li><code>lostdurability</code></li><li><code>itemdamaged</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/lethalcheck":{"h":"<h2>Lethal Check</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Evaluates whether the current damage event would kill the target entity. Returns true when the incoming damage exceeds the target&#x27;s current health plus absorption. Can optionally account for Totem of Undying protection.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>checktotems</code></td><td><code>ct</code>, <code>totemsafe</code>, <code>totemcheck</code></td><td>Whether to check if the target has a Totem of Undying before determining lethality</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>When <code>checktotems</code> is true and the target is holding a Totem of Undying, the condition returns false (damage is not considered lethal since the totem would save them).</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Only trigger soulbound on actual lethal hits\nSoulbound:\n  Skills:\n  - recoveritem{} @trigger ?lethalcheck ~onDamaged\n\n# Execute effect on killing blow (ignore totem protection)\nExecutionStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - particles{p=soul_fire_flame} @self ?lethalcheck{checktotems=false} ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>islethal</code></li><li><code>wouldkill</code></li><li><code>lethal</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/mench":{"h":"<h2>Has Enchantment</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks whether a player&#x27;s item slot has a specific enchantment at the given level. Supports vanilla, datapack, and MythicEnchants custom enchantments. When slot is <code>TRIGGER</code>, it scopes the condition to the enchanted item that fired the skill, with fallback to mainhand.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td><code>enchant</code>, <code>enchantment</code>, <code>e</code></td><td>The enchantment ID to check (namespaced or bare)</td><td><i>REQUIRED</i></td></tr><tr><td><code>level</code></td><td><code>lvl</code>, <code>l</code></td><td>Level or range to match</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (any level)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to evaluate</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Level Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches a specific level</td><td><code>2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a level range (inclusive)</td><td><code>2to3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>Matches levels above a value</td><td><code>&gt;1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>Matches levels at or above a value</td><td><code>&gt;=2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Matches levels below a value</td><td><code>&lt;4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>Matches levels at or below a value</td><td><code>&lt;=4</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>ConditionalSharpness:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=5} @trigger ?mench{id=SHARPNESS;level=&gt;=3} ~onAttack\n\n# Check for any level of Fire Aspect\nFireStrike:\n  Skills:\n  - ignite{ticks=60} @trigger ?mench{id=FIRE_ASPECT} ~onAttack\n\n# Check specific slot\nArmorCheck:\n  Skills:\n  - heal{a=2} @self ?mench{id=PROTECTION;level=4;slot=CHEST} ~onDamaged</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>enchant</code></li><li><code>enchantment</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:conditions/soulbounduses":{"h":"<h2>Check Recover Item</h2>\n<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>Checks the remaining <code>recoveritem</code> uses/charges on the trigger item. Used to conditionally execute skills based on how many soulbound charges remain.</p>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>uses</code></td><td><code>u</code>, <code>charges</code>, <code>c</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>v</code></td><td>Remaining uses to check against</td><td><code>&gt;0</code> (has charges)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\"><code>slot</code></a></td><td><code>s</code></td><td>The equipment slot to check</td><td><code>TRIGGER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Uses Formats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact</td><td>Matches exact remaining uses</td><td><code>3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>Matches a range (inclusive)</td><td><code>2to5</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater than</td><td>More than N uses remaining</td><td><code>&gt;1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Greater or equal</td><td>At least N uses remaining</td><td><code>&gt;=3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less than</td><td>Fewer than N uses remaining</td><td><code>&lt;1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Less or equal</td><td>At most N uses remaining</td><td><code>&lt;=2</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>SoulboundWarning:\n  Skills:\n  - message{m=&quot;&amp;cOnly 1 soulbound charge left!&quot;} @self ?checkrecoveritem{uses=1} ~onDamaged\n\nLowCharges:\n  Skills:\n  - particles{p=soul} @self ?checkrecoveritem{uses=&lt;=2} ~onTimer:40</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>recoveruses</code></li><li><code>soulbounduses</code></li><li><code>recovercharges</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:triggers/onapply":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment is applied to an item.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Trigger may only be utilized within the Skill configuration of an enchantment.\\</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>"},"enchants:triggers/onbowmiss":{"h":"<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder&#x27;s arrow hits a block or misses entirely</p>"},"enchants:triggers/onenchant":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder enchants via the vanilla enchanting table.</p>\n<blockquote><p>If using <a href=\"https://mythiccraft.io/index.php?resources/crucible-custom-items-armor-furniture-blocks-more.2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this trigger within item Skills.\\ This trigger may also be utilized within player skills powered by <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythicrpg/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicRPG</a></p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>"},"enchants:triggers/onremove":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment is removed from an item.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Trigger may only be utilized within the Skill configuration of an enchantment.\\</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>"},"enchants:triggers/onshieldblock":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder blocks an attack with a shield.</p>\n<blockquote><p>If using <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this trigger within item Skills.\\ This trigger may also be utilized within player skills powered by <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythicrpg/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicRPG</a></p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  # Enchantment Skill. Reflects 50% of blocked damage back at the attacker!\n  - skill{s=shieldreflect;sync=true} @self ~onShieldBlock\n\nshieldreflect:\n  Skills:\n  - damage{a=&lt;trigger.damage*0.5&gt;} @trigger\n  - particle{particle=BLOCK_CRACK;material=IRON_BLOCK;amount=10}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>onShieldBlock</code></li><li><code>onBlock</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:triggers/ontrample":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder Tramples farmland or turtle eggs.</p>\n<blockquote><p>If using <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a>, MythicEnchants also enables this trigger within item Skills.\\ This trigger may also be utilized within player skills powered by <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythicrpg/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicRPG</a></p></blockquote>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  # Enchantment Skill. Has a 50% chance to cancel the trample event!\n  - skill{s=canceltrample;sync=true} @self ~onTrample 0.5\n\ncanceltrample:\n  Skills:\n  - cancelevent\n  - particle{particle=CLOUD;amount=5}</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>onTrampleFarmland</code></li><li><code>onTrampleEgg</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:triggers/triggers":{"h":"<p>The Mythic-ecosystem triggers MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Triggers</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills.</p>\n<p>These registered triggers may be used outside of enchantments as well in some place.  Check specific triggers for details on their usage scope.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/mythiccrucible/-/wikis/Skills/Triggers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicCrucible</a> grants extensive item-related triggers, but many are redundant from base MythicMobs and already provided from it directly.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchantment Triggers</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onapply\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onApply\"><code>~onApply</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment is added to an item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onremove\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onRemove\"><code>~onRemove</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment is removed from an item</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onenchant\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onEnchant\"><code>~onEnchant</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder enchants via the vanilla enchanting table</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Player Triggers</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/ontrample\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onTrample\"><code>~onTrample</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment detects when farmland and turtle eggs have been trampled</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onshieldblock\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onShieldBlock\"><code>~onShieldBlock</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder blocks an attack with a shield.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Proj Triggers</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"triggers/onbowmiss\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Triggers/onbowmiss\"><code>~onBowMiss</code></a></td><td>When the enchantment&#x27;s wielder&#x27;s arrow hits a block or misses entirely</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code></p>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-description":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The description of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING description text of the triggering enchantment, as defined by its <code>Description:</code> field.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt;! &lt;skill.var.enchant-description&gt;&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_description&gt;</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-id":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The internal ID of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING internal ID of the triggering enchantment.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;The &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; enchantment was activated, as configured in the &lt;skill.var.enchant-id&gt; config!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_id&gt;</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-level":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the INTEGER value of the enchantment level.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; enchantment!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-maxlevel":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The maximum allowed level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the INTEGER value of the enchantment&#x27;s maximum possible level (regardless of its current level on trigger).</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;The &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; of &lt;trigger.name&gt; is Lvl &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; out of Max &lt;skill.var.enchant-maxlevel&gt;&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_maxlevel&gt;</code></li><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-maxlvl&gt;</code></li><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_maxlvl&gt;</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-name":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The display name of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING display name (with formatting and color) of the triggering enchantment.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt; enchantment!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_name&gt;</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-rarity":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The STRING tier of enchantment rarity of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the STRING value of the enchantment rarity.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment triggering this EnchantUse meta-skill will show some info about itself to its user.\n  - message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt; has activated their &lt;skill.var.enchant-rarity&gt; enchantment, &lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt; &lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;!&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_rarity&gt;</code></li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/enchant-totallevel":{"h":"<h3>Description</h3>\n<p>The summed level of the triggering enchantment across every one of the caster&#x27;s equipped slots (hand, off-hand, head, chest, legs, feet).</p>\n<blockquote><p>Targeter may only be utilized within a skill tree triggered by an enchantment.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>Will return the INT total of all levels of the triggering enchantment currently worn by the caster — e.g. four armor pieces each carrying level 3 of the enchantment returns <code>12</code>, not <code>3</code>.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>EnchantUse:\n  Skills:\n  # An enchantment with the same ID on multiple worn pieces scales its effect off the combined total, firing once rather than once per piece.\n  - damage{a=&lt;skill.var.enchant-total-levels&gt;} @target ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<h3>Aliases</h3>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_total_levels&gt;</code> for it</li></ul>"},"enchants:placeholders/papi-placeholders":{"h":"<h3>PlaceholderAPI Placeholders</h3>\n<p>When <a href=\"https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/placeholderapi.6245/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PlaceholderAPI</a> is installed, MythicEnchants registers the following PAPI placeholders:</p>\n<h3>PlaceholderAPI</h3>\n<p>Registered under both <code>%mythicenchants_...%</code> and <code>%mench_...%</code></p>\n<h4>Global</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>total</code></td><td>Total registered enchantment count</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchseed</code></td><td>Current enchanting seed for the placeholder&#x27;s player</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchseed_pin</code></td><td>Currently pinned enchantment id for the placeholder&#x27;s player</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_name_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Display name of enchant <code>&lt;id&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_description_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Description of enchant <code>&lt;id&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_rarity_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Rarity enum name</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_rarity_color_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Rarity color hex string</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_rarity_display_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Colored rarity display name</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_total_level_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Colored rarity display name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Slot-based (<code>&lt;slot&gt;_...</code>)</h4>\n<p>Slots: <code>mainhand</code>/<code>hand</code>, <code>offhand</code>, <code>head</code>/<code>helm</code>, <code>chest</code>, <code>legs</code>, <code>feet</code>/<code>boots</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_total</code> / <code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_count</code></td><td>Number of enchantments on that slot&#x27;s item</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchants</code></td><td>Comma-joined list of enchant IDs on that slot&#x27;s item</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_has_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td><code>true</code>/<code>false</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_level_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Level of enchant <code>&lt;id&gt;</code> on that slot (<code>0</code> if absent)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;</code></td><td>Enchant ID at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code> (1-indexed)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;_name</code></td><td>Display name of the enchant at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;_level</code></td><td>Level of the enchant at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;slot&gt;_enchant_&lt;n&gt;_description</code> / <code>_desc</code></td><td>Description of the enchant at index <code>&lt;n&gt;</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Example: <code>%mythicenchants_hand_enchant_1_name%</code>, <code>%mench_helm_has_minecraft:protection%</code></p>"},"enchants:placeholders/placeholders":{"h":"<h2>Placeholders</h2>\n<p>The Mythic-ecosystem placeholders MythicEnchants provides.  These expand on <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Placeholders\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMob Placeholders</a>, which typically may be used as expected within enchantment skills, including in-line condition evaluations.</p>\n<p>Some Mythic triggers contain <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Placeholders#variable-placeholders\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Integrated Placeholders</a> to provide additional functionality, such as <code>&lt;skill.var.damage-amount&gt;</code> from attack and damage events to evaluate the damage delivered.  Many in-line placeholder usage, especially with variables, require <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Premium-Features\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic Premium</a>.</p>\n<p>These registered placeholders may be used outside of enchantments as well, such as a mob&#x27;s skills evaluating a player&#x27;s item for enchantments or durability.</p>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"info/dependencies\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Info/Dependencies\">MythicCrucible</a> also grants item-related placeholders!</p></blockquote>\n<blockquote><p>All variables support both dash (<code>-</code>) and underscore (<code>_</code>) separators interchangeably.\\ e.g. <code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;skill.var.enchant_level&gt;</code> are equivalent.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchantment Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-id\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-ID\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-id&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The ID of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-rarity\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Rarity\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-rarity&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The rarity of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-name\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Name\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-name&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The display name of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-description\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Description\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-description&gt;</code></a></td><td>STRING</td><td>The description of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-level\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Level\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;</code></a></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>The level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-maxlevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-MaxLevel\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-maxlevel&gt;</code></a></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>The maximum level of the enchantment that triggered the skill tree</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-totallevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-TotalLevel\"><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-total-levels&gt;</code></a></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Will return the INT total of all levels of the triggering enchantment currently worn</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p><code>&lt;skill.var.enchant-*&gt;</code> placeholders only reflect the <b>currently firing</b> enchantment&#x27;s trigger context. To look up a specific enchantment by ID (any enchantment, not just the one that triggered the skill), use the <code>&lt;enchant.ID.field&gt;</code> placeholders below instead.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchant Definition Placeholders</h3>\n<p>Look up any registered enchantment&#x27;s definition data by ID — independent of any trigger context, usable anywhere a MythicMobs placeholder is valid.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.name&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Display name of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.description&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;enchant.ID.desc&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Description of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.maxlvl&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;enchant.ID.maxlevel&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Maximum level of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.minlvl&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;enchant.ID.minlevel&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Minimum level of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.rarity&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Rarity enum name of enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.ID.totallevel&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Will return the INT total of all levels of the named enchantment currently worn by the placeholder&#x27;s entity`</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>ID</code> may be a bare key (resolved against the plugin&#x27;s default namespace, then tried raw) or a fully-qualified <code>namespace:key</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>- message{msg=&quot;&lt;trigger.name&gt;&#x27;s target has &lt;enchant.frost_bite.name&gt;: &lt;enchant.frost_bite.description&gt;&quot;} @self</code></pre>\n<h4>Slot-Aware Enchant Placeholders</h4>\n<p>Reads the enchantment&#x27;s level directly off the placeholder context entity&#x27;s equipped item for a given slot — works for any enchantment ID, not just the one that triggered the skill.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.SLOT.ID.level&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Level of enchantment <code>ID</code> on the entity&#x27;s <code>SLOT</code> item (<code>0</code> if absent)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;enchant.SLOT.ID.has&gt;</code></td><td>BOOLEAN</td><td>Whether the entity&#x27;s <code>SLOT</code> item has enchantment <code>ID</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Valid <code>SLOT</code> values: <code>mainhand</code>/<code>hand</code>, <code>offhand</code>, <code>head</code>/<code>helm</code>/<code>helmet</code>, <code>chest</code>/<code>chestplate</code>, <code>legs</code>/<code>leggings</code>, <code>feet</code>/<code>boots</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>- message{msg=&quot;You have Frost Bite &lt;enchant.mainhand.frost_bite.level&gt; on your weapon!&quot;} @self ?enchant.mainhand.frost_bite.has</code></pre>\n<h3>Bookshelves Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;caster.var.menchbookshelves&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>The scanned <b>table power</b> — the same <code>count</code> the table feeds into its slot equations. Uses the config&#x27;s scan shape. Uncapped by design (caps live at the slot level)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.radial.4&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Table power, but scanning a chebyshev ring <code>1..4</code> (Y <code>0..1</code>) instead of the config shape</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.radial.2.5&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Table power, chebyshev ring <code>inner=2..outer=5</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.cuboid.3&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Table power, full cube radius <code>3</code> (every <code>dx, dy, dz</code> in <code>-3..3</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.slot.1&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 1&#x27;s <b>capped base level</b>: slot equation (<code>count</code> = power) → per-slot <code>slot-cap</code> → <code>max-base-level</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.slot.2&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 2&#x27;s capped base level</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.slot.3&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 3&#x27;s capped base level</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;bookshelves.radial.4.slot.2&gt;</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Slot 2&#x27;s base level computed from the radial-4 scan</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Caster Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.player-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The wielder&#x27;s current health</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.player-max-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The wielder&#x27;s maximum health</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.fall-distance&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The wielder&#x27;s current accumulated fall distance in blocks</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Target Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.target-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The skill target&#x27;s current health (when a target entity is present)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.target-max-health&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td>The skill target&#x27;s maximum health (when a target entity is present)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Trigger-Specific Placeholders</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Trigger(s)</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.damage&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td><code>~onDamaged</code></td><td>The incoming damage amount from the current damage event</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.item-attack&gt;</code></td><td>FLOAT</td><td><code>~onAttack</code></td><td>The equipment&#x27;s attack damage value</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.equip-slot&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Most triggers</td><td>The equipment slot of the enchanted item (e.g. <code>HAND</code>, <code>CHEST</code>, <code>FEET</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Enchant Apply/Remove Trigger Placeholders</h3>\n<p>These are injected only during <code>~onEnchantApply</code> and <code>~onEnchantRemove</code> triggers:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Placeholder</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantments-applied&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Number of enchantments applied (<code>~onEnchantApply</code> only)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantments-removed&gt;</code></td><td>INTEGER</td><td>Number of enchantments removed (<code>~onEnchantRemove</code> only)</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantments&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Comma-separated list of enchantment IDs applied or removed</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantment-source&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>Source of the enchantment change: <code>TABLE</code>, <code>ANVIL</code>, <code>COMMAND</code>, or <code>GRINDSTONE</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;skill.var.enchantment_applied.N&gt;</code></td><td>STRING</td><td>The Nth enchantment ID in the change (1-based index)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Math Expressions</h3>\n<p>MythicEnchants provides a <code>&lt;math:EXPR&gt;</code> placeholder for evaluating math expressions inline. Any of the above variables can be referenced inside math expressions using their underscore form.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4>\n<p>Enchantment File:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>&lt;math:EXPRESSION&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>Metaskill or Skills File (Requires MM Premium):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>&lt;math.EXPRESSION&gt;</code></pre>\n<h4>Available Variables in Math</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>enchant_level</code></td><td>Level of the triggering enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><code>enchant_maxlevel</code></td><td>Maximum level of the triggering enchantment</td></tr><tr><td><code>player_health</code></td><td>Caster&#x27;s current health</td></tr><tr><td><code>player_max_health</code></td><td>Caster&#x27;s maximum health</td></tr><tr><td><code>fall_distance</code></td><td>Caster&#x27;s accumulated fall distance in blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>target_health</code></td><td>Target&#x27;s current health (0 if no target)</td></tr><tr><td><code>target_max_health</code></td><td>Target&#x27;s maximum health (0 if no target)</td></tr><tr><td><code>damage</code></td><td>Incoming/outgoing damage value (0 if not applicable)</td></tr><tr><td><code>item_attack</code></td><td>Item attack value (0 if not applicable)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Supported Functions</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>min(a, b)</code></td><td>Returns the smaller of two values</td></tr><tr><td><code>max(a, b)</code></td><td>Returns the larger of two values</td></tr><tr><td><code>clamp(v, min, max)</code></td><td>Clamps a value between min and max</td></tr><tr><td><code>round(x)</code></td><td>Rounds to the nearest integer</td></tr><tr><td><code>floor(x)</code></td><td>Rounds down to the nearest integer</td></tr><tr><td><code>ceil(x)</code></td><td>Rounds up to the nearest integer</td></tr><tr><td><code>abs(x)</code></td><td>Returns the absolute value</td></tr><tr><td><code>sqrt(x)</code></td><td>Square root</td></tr><tr><td><code>random(min, max)</code></td><td>Random float between min and max</td></tr><tr><td><code>randomInt(min, max)</code></td><td>Random integer between min and max (inclusive)</td></tr><tr><td><code>lerp(a, b, t)</code></td><td>Linear interpolation between a and b by factor t</td></tr><tr><td><code>step(edge, x)</code></td><td>Returns 1 if x &gt;= edge, otherwise 0</td></tr><tr><td><code>sin(x)</code>, <code>cos(x)</code>, <code>tan(x)</code></td><td>Trigonometric functions</td></tr><tr><td><code>log(x)</code>, <code>log2(x)</code>, <code>log10(x)</code></td><td>Logarithmic functions</td></tr><tr><td><code>signum(x)</code></td><td>Returns -1, 0, or 1 based on sign</td></tr><tr><td><code>logb(x, base)</code></td><td>Logarithm with custom base</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Supported Operators</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operator</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>+</code> <code>-</code> <code>*</code> <code>/</code> <code>^</code></td><td>Standard arithmetic</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;</code> <code>&lt;=</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>&gt;=</code> <code>==</code></td><td>Comparison (returns 1 or 0)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"},"enchants:items/slots":{"h":"<p>The valid slots that can be defined in various skill operations.</p>\n<blockquote><p>These slots correspond to <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/EquipSlot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic&#x27;s Slot Operations</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>Aliases</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>HEAD</td><td>HELMET, HELM, HAT</td></tr><tr><td>CHEST</td><td>CHESTPIECE, CHESTPLATE, BODY</td></tr><tr><td>LEGS</td><td>LEGGINGS, PANTS</td></tr><tr><td>FEET</td><td>BOOTS, SHOES</td></tr><tr><td>HAND</td><td>MAINHAND, WEAPON</td></tr><tr><td>OFFHAND</td><td>SHIELD</td></tr><tr><td>TRIGGER</td><td>ITEM</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p><code>TRIGGER</code> is unique to MythicEnchants, and refers to the item that triggered the skill.  This is only usable within MythicEnchant placeholders/skills.</p></blockquote>"},"enchants:enchants/attributes":{"h":"<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>The <code>Attributes</code> section is a declarative shorthand for applying item attribute modifiers without writing full skill line syntax. Each entry generates a pair of synthetic skill lines — one on <code>~onEnchant</code> to apply the modifier, and one on <code>~onEnchantRemove</code> to clean it up — equivalent to using <code>enchantitemattribute</code> manually in <code>Skills</code>.</p>\n<p>Attribute modifiers are written directly onto the item&#x27;s metadata, so they persist across sessions, appear in the item tooltip, and stack correctly with the item&#x27;s base attributes.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Attributes:\n    &lt;SlotGroup&gt;:\n      - &lt;ATTRIBUTE&gt; &lt;AMOUNT&gt; [OPERATION]</code></pre>\n<p>Each line under a slot group follows this format:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ATTRIBUTE</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The attribute name (see <span class=\"ilink\">Attributes</span>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AMOUNT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>A numeric value or <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expression</td></tr><tr><td><code>OPERATION</code></td><td>No</td><td>The modifier operation (see <span class=\"ilink\">Operations</span>). Defaults to <code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Attributes:\n    MainHand:\n      - MAX_HEALTH 4\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE 2 ADD_NUMBER\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*0.5&gt; ADD_NUMBER\n    Any:\n      - ARMOR 2\n      - ARMOR_TOUGHNESS 1 ADD_NUMBER</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Slot Groups</h4>\n<p>The slot group key determines which equipment slot the attribute modifier is active in. Accepts any valid <code>EquipmentSlotGroup</code> name (case-insensitive).</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>MainHand</code></td><td>Active when held in the main hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>OffHand</code></td><td>Active when held in the off hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>Head</code></td><td>Active when worn on the head</td></tr><tr><td><code>Chest</code></td><td>Active when worn on the chest</td></tr><tr><td><code>Legs</code></td><td>Active when worn on the legs</td></tr><tr><td><code>Feet</code></td><td>Active when worn on the feet</td></tr><tr><td><code>Armor</code></td><td>Active in any armor slot</td></tr><tr><td><code>Any</code></td><td>Active in any slot</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h4>Attribute Names</h4>\n<p>Attributes are resolved against the Minecraft attribute registry. Both the full namespaced form and bare shorthand are accepted. The <code>generic_</code> prefix is stripped automatically, so <code>generic_max_health</code>, <code>max_health</code>, and <code>minecraft:generic.max_health</code> all resolve to the same attribute.</p>\n<p>Common attributes:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>MAX_HEALTH</code></td><td>Maximum health points</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Melee attack damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_SPEED</code></td><td>Attack speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_KNOCKBACK</code></td><td>Knockback applied on hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR</code></td><td>Armor points</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR_TOUGHNESS</code></td><td>Armor toughness</td></tr><tr><td><code>KNOCKBACK_RESISTANCE</code></td><td>Resistance to knockback</td></tr><tr><td><code>MOVEMENT_SPEED</code></td><td>Movement speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>FLYING_SPEED</code></td><td>Flying speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>BLOCK_BREAK_SPEED</code></td><td>Block breaking speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>LUCK</code></td><td>Luck</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Any attribute registered in the Minecraft attribute registry can be used. Use the full <code>namespace:key</code> form for modded or non-generic attributes.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Operations</h4>\n<p>Controls how the amount is applied to the base attribute value.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Aliases</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADD_NUMBER</code></td><td><code>ADD</code>, <code>FLAT</code>, <code>BASE</code></td><td>Adds a flat value to the base</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADD_SCALAR</code></td><td><code>SCALAR</code>, <code>PERCENT</code>, <code>PERCENT_BASE</code></td><td>Multiplies the base by <code>(1 + amount)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>MULTIPLY_SCALAR_1</code></td><td><code>MULTIPLY</code>, <code>PERCENT_TOTAL</code></td><td>Multiplies the total (after all additions) by <code>(1 + amount)</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Defaults to <code>ADD_NUMBER</code> if omitted.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Math Expressions</h4>\n<p>The <code>AMOUNT</code> field supports <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expressions, allowing level-scaling modifiers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Attributes:\n    MainHand:\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*1.5&gt; ADD_NUMBER\n      - MAX_HEALTH &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt; ADD_NUMBER</code></pre>\n<p>All standard enchantment variables are available: <code>enchant_level</code>, <code>enchant_maxlevel</code>, etc.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Notes</h4>\n<ul><li>Modifiers are written into the item metadata and visible in the tooltip.</li><li>If the item already has a base modifier for the same attribute, operation, and slot group (e.g. a sword&#x27;s default attack damage), the <code>Attributes</code> system will absorb and combine it rather than duplicating it, then restore the original on removal.</li><li><code>Attributes</code> generates <code>enchantitemattribute</code> skill lines internally. For more advanced control — such as targeting a specific item slot, using <code>SET</code> vs <code>ADD</code> mode, or custom modifier keys — use <code>enchantitemattribute</code> directly in <code>Skills</code> instead.</li></ul>\n<p><code>`</code></p>"},"enchants:enchants/custom-enchantments":{"h":"<h4>File Locations</h4>\n<p>The primary location custom enchantments are stored is in the <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/enchantments/</code> folder.  Enchantments may also be organized into and loaded from the <code>../enchantments/</code> folder of any <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Packs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic Pack</a>.</p>\n<blockquote><p>A typical custom enchantment might be located in <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/enchantments/holy_shine.yml</code>.\\ Enchantment files may include multiple enchantments, such as <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/enchantments/lunar.yml</code> containing the <code>lunar_blessing</code> and <code>lunar_light</code> enchantments.\\ A Mythic Pack location might be <code>/plugins/MythicMobs/packs/lemons_enchants/enchantments/sour_strike.yml</code>, featuring the <code>sour_strike</code> enchantment from the &quot;Lemon&#x27;s Enchants&quot; pack.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Enchantment Elements</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchantment-config\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchantment-Config\">Complete Enchantment Config</a><ul><li><span class=\"ilink\">Internal Name</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Display Name</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Description</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Min Level</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Max Level</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Rarity</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Anvil Cost</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Tags</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Conflicting Enchantments</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Options</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Valid Slots</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Supported Items</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Primary Items</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Enchanting</span><ul><li><span class=\"ilink\">Weight</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Min &amp; Max Cost</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Promised</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Book Offer</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Reagent</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Conditions</span></li></ul></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Attributes</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Skills</span></li></ul></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Examples</span></li></ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>General Settings</h3>\n<h4>Internal Name</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The internal string identifier for the enchantment. Must be a unique name using valid characters and no spaces. Only visible in configurations.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-id\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-ID\"><code>enchant-id</code></a> placeholder returns this value in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Display Name</h4>\n<p>The visible name of the enchantment, shown in rich text locations.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-name\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Name\"><code>enchant-name</code></a> placeholder returns this value, including its colors and formatting, in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Description</h4>\n<p>An optional description for the enchantment. Used for informational purposes.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Description: &quot;Heals the player on attack.&quot;</code></pre>\n<h4>Min Level</h4>\n<p>The minimum level the enchantment starts at. Defaults to <code>1</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MinLevel: 1</code></pre>\n<h4>Max Level</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The maximum level the enchantment is permitted to reach. Must be a whole number between 1 and 255.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MaxLevel: 5</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-maxlevel\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-MaxLevel\"><code>enchant-maxlevel</code></a> placeholder returns this integer in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Rarity</h4>\n<p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"rarities\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Rarities\">rarity tier</a> assigned to the enchantment. Creates groupings beyond weight, such as being able to roll a &quot;RARE&quot; enchantment specifically.\\ Rarities are defined in a <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"rarities\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Rarities\">Rarities</a> file.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Rarity: UNCOMMON</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"placeholders/enchant-rarity\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Placeholders/Enchant-Rarity\"><code>enchant-rarity</code></a> placeholder returns this value in enchantment skills.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Anvil Cost</h4>\n<p>The experience cost associated with the enchantment during anvil operations.\\ Half of this value is used for operations on an enchanted book. This cost is multiplied by the enchantment&#x27;s level.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  AnvilCost: 3</code></pre>\n<h4>Tags</h4>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">enchantment tags</a> assigned to the enchantment. Configures many behaviors such as loot table inclusion, exclusivity groups, and more.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Tags:\n    - minecraft:on_random_loot  # appears in general vanilla chest/mob loot\n    - special_group             # example custom tag for grouping</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>Unlike other config areas, tags do not require the <code>#minecraft:tag</code> syntax — this field takes plain tag name inputs.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Conflicting Enchantments</h4>\n<p>Enchantments considered mutually exclusive with this enchantment. Accepts all lowercase enchantment IDs or <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">enchantment tags</a>. Must include namespace in enchantment ID.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  ConflictingEnchants:\n    - &#x27;#minecraft:exclusive_set/damage&#x27;\n    - minecraft:mending</code></pre>\n<h4>Options</h4>\n<p>A configuration section for behavioral flags.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Enabled</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Enables or disables the enchantment entirely</td></tr><tr><td><code>Cursed</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Applies the <code>#minecraft:curse</code> tag — red name, prevents removal</td></tr><tr><td><code>Treasure</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Applies the <code>#minecraft:treasure</code> tag</td></tr><tr><td><code>RandomLoot</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can appear in random loot</td></tr><tr><td><code>Tradeable</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can be traded by villagers</td></tr><tr><td><code>TradedEquipment</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can appear on villager-traded equipment</td></tr><tr><td><code>MobSpawnEquipment</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Whether this enchantment can appear on mob spawn equipment</td></tr><tr><td><code>PVP</code></td><td><i>(unset)</i></td><td>Override PVP behavior for this enchantment&#x27;s skills</td></tr><tr><td><code>StrictMythicItems</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Restrict application to only the exact Mythic items listed in <code>PrimaryItems</code> (see <span class=\"ilink\">Primary Items</span>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Enabled: true\n    Cursed: false\n    Treasure: false\n    RandomLoot: true\n    Tradeable: true\n    StrictMythicItems: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Valid Slots</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The equipped <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"items/slots\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Items/Slots\">slot(s)</a> the enchantment takes effect in..</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  ValidSlots:\n    - MAINHAND\n    - OFF_HAND</code></pre>\n<h4>Supported Items</h4>\n<p><b>❗️Required.</b> The item tag defining which items this enchantment can be applied to. Accepts a <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Item_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">datapack item tag</a> reference.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:swords&#x27;</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p>Enchantments missing this field will fail to load.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Primary Items</h4>\n<p>The specific item material IDs or <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Item_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">item tags</a> that are the preferred items for this enchantment. Shown first in the enchanting table UI.\\ Also accepts <code>mythic:ID</code> entries to reference MythicMobs/Crucible items by their internal ID.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  PrimaryItems:\n    - &#x27;#minecraft:swords&#x27;\n    - minecraft:diamond_axe\n    - minecraft:netherite_axe\n    - mythic:MY_MYTHIC_ITEM_ID</code></pre>\n<blockquote><p><code>mythic:</code> entries are stored separately and enforced at runtime — datapacks match by material only and cannot distinguish Mythic items from plain ones of the same type.\\ To restrict the enchantment exclusively to the listed Mythic items (blocking plain items of the same material), set <code>Options.StrictMythicItems: true</code>.</p></blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h3><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchanting-table\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table\">Enchanting</a></h3>\n<p>Configure the enchanting weight and table behaviors of the enchantment.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10\n    MinCost: 15\n    MaxCost: 50\n    Promised: true\n    BookOffer: true\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n    Conditions:\n      - outside</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Attributes</h3>\n<p>A declarative shorthand for applying attribute modifiers via synthetic skill lines, without writing full skill syntax. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/attributes\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes\">Attributes</a>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Attributes:\n    MainHand:\n      - ATTACK_DAMAGE 2</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>MythicStats</h3>\n<p>A declarative shorthand for applying MythicMobs stat modifiers via synthetic skill lines, without writing full skill syntax. See <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/mythicstats\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/MythicStats\">MythicStats</a>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Stats:\n    - POWER 10\n    - CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE 5 ADDITIVE\n    - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Skills</h3>\n<p>The primary action section of your enchantment, using the <a href=\"https://git.lumine.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/Skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mythic Skill System</a> to define what the enchantment does and when.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Skills:\n    - heal{a=0.5*&lt;skill.var.enchant-level&gt;;cooldown=5} @self ~onAttack</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>CONFIG.YML SNIPPET</code> <code>`</code></p>"},"enchants:enchants/enchantdata":{"h":"<h2>EnchantData</h2>\n<p><code>EnchantData:</code> is an optional section inside any enchantment YAML that lets you declaratively define <b>vanilla Minecraft datapack effect components</b> — the same JSON that lives in <code>data/&lt;namespace&gt;/enchantment/&lt;key&gt;.json</code>. Instead of writing raw JSON you write YAML; MythicEnchants validates it and generates the correct datapack file at startup.</p>\n<p>Any parse error (typo in a key, missing required field, etc.) is printed to the server log and <b>blocks that enchantment from being written to the datapack entirely</b> until fixed. Other enchantments are unaffected.</p>\n<blockquote><p><b>Minecraft wiki references</b></p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#JSON_format\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Enchantment definition JSON format</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Effect_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Effect components overview</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Loot_table#Conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Loot table conditions (predicates/requirements)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Entity_effects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity effects</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute#Modifiers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attribute modifiers</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Particles#Types_of_particles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Particle types</a></li><li><a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Sounds.json#Sound_events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sound events</a></li></ul></blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h3>Table of Contents</h3>\n<ol><li><span class=\"ilink\">Version compatibility</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">How it fits together</span></li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Value providers</span> — how numbers are expressed</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Requirements / predicates</span> — conditional gating</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Value effect components</span> — scalar boosts</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Bare value components</span> — crossbow &amp; trident timing</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Entity effect components</span> — on-hit, on-tick, etc.</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Entity effect types</span> — what happens</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Attribute effects</span> — stat modifiers</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Flag components</span> — boolean toggles</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Special components</span> — sounds</li><li><span class=\"ilink\">Full examples</span></li></ol>\n<hr>\n<h3>Version compatibility</h3>\n<p>MythicEnchants detects the running server version at startup and generates datapacks at the correct pack format automatically.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Server version</th><th>Pack format</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1.21.11</td><td>94</td><td>Supported. <code>post_piercing_attack</code> and <code>damage_immunity</code> skipped with a warning.</td></tr><tr><td>26.1.x</td><td>101</td><td>Supported. Same component restrictions as 94.</td></tr><tr><td>26.2+</td><td>107</td><td>Full support for all components.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Predicate key format</h4>\n<p>Minecraft changed how sub-keys inside <code>entity_properties</code> predicates are named in pack format 107:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key purpose</th><th>Pre-107 (1.21.11, 26.1)</th><th>107+ (26.2)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Entity flags</td><td><code>flags</code></td><td><code>minecraft:flags</code></td></tr><tr><td>Location check</td><td><code>location</code></td><td><code>minecraft:location</code></td></tr><tr><td>Entity type</td><td><code>type</code></td><td><code>minecraft:entity_type</code></td></tr><tr><td>Type-specific data</td><td><code>type_specific</code></td><td><code>minecraft:type_specific</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Always write predicates in the 26.2 namespaced form.</b> MythicEnchants automatically rewrites them to the correct bare-key form when generating datapacks for servers on format &lt; 107. You never need to maintain two versions of a predicate.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Write this on any server version — MythicEnchants handles the rest\nrequirements:\n  condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n  entity: this\n  predicate:\n    minecraft:flags:\n      is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Components not available before 26.2</h4>\n<p>These are skipped with a server log warning on format &lt; 107. The enchantment still loads normally — only the datapack component is omitted.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Minimum version</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>post_piercing_attack</code></td><td>26.2 (pack format 107) — added for Lunge</td></tr><tr><td><code>damage_immunity</code></td><td>26.2 (pack format 107)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h3>How it fits together</h3>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>my_enchant:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;6My Enchant&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sword&#x27;\n\n  EnchantData:\n    # Everything under here is datapack generation\n    damage:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: 0.5\n        perLevel: 0.5\n\n  Skills:\n    - ... # normal MythicEnchants skill lines still work alongside EnchantData</code></pre>\n<p><code>EnchantData:</code> and <code>Skills:</code> are independent — you can use both, either, or neither.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Value providers</h3>\n<p>A <b>value provider</b> describes how a number is calculated, usually based on enchantment level. Used anywhere a numeric field appears (value effects, attribute amounts, entity effect parameters, etc.).</p>\n<h4>linear</h4>\n<p>Grows linearly with level. <code>base</code> is the value at level 1; <code>perLevel</code> is added for each level above 1.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: linear\n  base: 1.0\n  perLevel: 0.5\n# level 1 = 1.0, level 2 = 1.5, level 3 = 2.0</code></pre>\n<p>Shorthand (same thing, no <code>type:</code> needed):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>base: 1.0\nperLevel: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h4>constant</h4>\n<p>Fixed value regardless of level.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: constant\n  value: 2.5</code></pre>\n<p>Bare number shorthand (only on top-level effect keys, not inside nested sections):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>fishing_luck_bonus: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>levels_squared</h4>\n<p>Value = <code>(level - 1)² + added</code>. Vanilla uses this for Protection.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: levels_squared\n  added: 1.0\n# level 1 = 1, level 2 = 2, level 3 = 5, level 4 = 10</code></pre>\n<h4>lookup</h4>\n<p>Returns a fixed value per level from a list. If the level exceeds the list length, <code>fallback</code> is used.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: lookup\n  values: [1.0, 2.5, 4.5, 7.0]\n  fallback: 7.0   # also accepts a nested value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>clamped</h4>\n<p>Clamps another value provider to a <code>[min, max]</code> range.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: clamped\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: 0.0\n    perLevel: 2.0\n  min: 0.0\n  max: 6.0</code></pre>\n<h4>fraction</h4>\n<p>Divides one value provider by another. Vanilla uses this for Sweeping Edge.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: fraction\n  numerator:\n    type: linear\n    base: 1.0\n    perLevel: 1.0\n  denominator:\n    type: linear\n    base: 2.0\n    perLevel: 1.0\n# level 1 = 1/2, level 2 = 2/3, level 3 = 3/4</code></pre>\n<p>Bare numbers work for numerator/denominator too:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: fraction\n  numerator: 1.0\n  denominator: 3.0</code></pre>\n<h4>exponent</h4>\n<p>Raises <code>base</code> to the power of <code>power</code>. Both accept nested value providers or bare numbers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: exponent\n  base: 2.0\n  power:\n    type: linear\n    base: 1.0\n    perLevel: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>formula (math)</h4>\n<p>Evaluates a math expression once per level (1 through <code>MaxLevel</code>) and bakes the results into a <code>minecraft:lookup</code> table — vanilla&#x27;s JSON format has no arbitrary-formula value type, so MythicEnchants resolves the expression ahead of time at datapack generation rather than at runtime. Uses the same expression engine (exp4j) and function set as <code>&lt;math:...&gt;</code> skill-line tokens — see the class doc on <code>MenchMathParser</code> for the full operator/function list (<code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>clamp</code>, <code>sqrt</code>, <code>sin</code>, <code>round</code>, <code>lerp</code>, etc.).</p>\n<p>Available variables: <code>level</code> (current enchantment level), <code>max_level</code> (the enchant&#x27;s <code>MaxLevel</code>).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>value:\n  type: formula\n  expression: &quot;1 + sqrt(level) * 2&quot;\n# level 1 = 3, level 2 = 3.83, level 3 = 4.46, ...</code></pre>\n<p><code>math</code> is accepted as an alias for <code>type: formula</code>. A parse/eval error at any level is logged and that level falls back to <code>0</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Requirements / predicates</h3>\n<p>Any effect entry can include an optional <code>requirements:</code> block. This is a standard <b>Minecraft Predicate</b> written as YAML — it is serialised directly to JSON without any schema validation, so you can use the full condition vocabulary from the wiki.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Predicate\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Predicate</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage:\n  value:\n    base: 2.0\n    perLevel: 1.0\n  requirements:\n    condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n    entity: this\n    predicate:\n      minecraft:flags:\n        is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<p>Multiple conditions — wrap them in <code>minecraft:all_of</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>requirements:\n  condition: minecraft:all_of\n  terms:\n    - condition: minecraft:random_chance\n      chance: 0.25\n    - condition: minecraft:weather_check\n      thundering: true</code></pre>\n<p><b>Always write predicates in the 26.2 namespaced form</b> (<code>minecraft:flags</code>, <code>minecraft:location</code>, <code>minecraft:entity_type</code>, etc.). MythicEnchants automatically rewrites them to the correct bare-key form for servers running pre-107 pack formats. See <span class=\"ilink\">Version compatibility</span> for details.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Value effect components</h3>\n<p>These are <b>conditional arrays</b> — each entry has an effect (the number) and an optional requirements predicate. Multiple entries are evaluated in order; all matching entries are summed.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Value_effect_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Value effect components</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>What it affects</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>damage</code></td><td>Extra damage dealt</td></tr><tr><td><code>damage_protection</code></td><td>Damage reduction (Protection family)</td></tr><tr><td><code>armor_effectiveness</code></td><td>How much armor helps against this damage source</td></tr><tr><td><code>knockback</code></td><td>Knockback strength on hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>smash_damage_per_fallen_block</code></td><td>Bonus damage per block fallen before impact (Density)</td></tr><tr><td><code>equipment_drops</code></td><td>Chance modifier for mob equipment drops</td></tr><tr><td><code>ammo_use</code></td><td>Ammo consumption modifier (Infinity uses 0)</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_piercing</code></td><td>How many entities a projectile can pierce (Piercing)</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_count</code></td><td>Number of projectiles fired (Multishot)</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_spread</code></td><td>Spread angle of projectiles in degrees</td></tr><tr><td><code>block_experience</code></td><td>XP dropped from breaking blocks (Fortune)</td></tr><tr><td><code>mob_experience</code></td><td>XP dropped from killing mobs (Looting)</td></tr><tr><td><code>repair_with_xp</code></td><td>Item repair rate from XP (Mending)</td></tr><tr><td><code>item_damage</code></td><td>Durability damage dealt to the item</td></tr><tr><td><code>trident_return_acceleration</code></td><td>Loyalty return speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>fishing_time_reduction</code></td><td>Reduction in fishing wait time (Lure)</td></tr><tr><td><code>fishing_luck_bonus</code></td><td>Luck bonus for fishing loot table (Luck of the Sea)</td></tr><tr><td><code>location_changed</code></td><td>Fires when the player moves to a new block (Frost Walker)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Single entry (most common)</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage:\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: 0.5\n    perLevel: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h4>With requirements</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage_protection:\n  value:\n    type: levels_squared\n    added: 1.0\n  requirements:\n    condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n    entity: this\n    predicate:\n      minecraft:flags:\n        is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Multiple gated entries</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage:\n  entries:\n    - value:\n        type: constant\n        value: 2.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.5\n    - value:\n        base: 0.5\n        perLevel: 0.25</code></pre>\n<h4>Bare number shorthand</h4>\n<p>Expands to a constant value with no requirements:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>fishing_luck_bonus: 2.0</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Bare value components</h3>\n<p>These two components take a <b>single bare value object</b> in the datapack JSON — not an array of conditional entries. You cannot add multiple gated entries; use them for a simple scalar override.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:crossbow_charge_time\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">crossbow_charge_time</a>, <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:trident_spin_attack_strength\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">trident_spin_attack_strength</a></p></blockquote>\n<h4>crossbow_charge_time</h4>\n<p>Changes crossbow charge time. Negative values make it faster (vanilla Quick Charge: −0.25 per level).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charge_time:\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: -0.25\n    perLevel: -0.25</code></pre>\n<p>Shorthand:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charge_time: -0.75</code></pre>\n<h4>trident_spin_attack_strength</h4>\n<p>Strength of the trident spin attack (Riptide).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>trident_spin_attack_strength:\n  value:\n    type: linear\n    base: 1.5\n    perLevel: 0.75</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Entity effect components</h3>\n<p>These fire in response to game events. Each entry specifies <b>who carries the enchantment</b> (<code>enchanted</code>), <b>who is affected</b> (<code>affected</code>), the <b>effect type</b>, and an optional <code>requirements</code> predicate.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Entity_effect_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity effect components</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>When it fires</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>post_attack</code></td><td>After a melee attack connects</td></tr><tr><td><code>tick</code></td><td>Every game tick while equipped in a valid slot</td></tr><tr><td><code>hit_block</code></td><td>When a projectile hits a block</td></tr><tr><td><code>projectile_spawned</code></td><td>When a projectile is fired</td></tr><tr><td><code>post_piercing_attack</code></td><td>After a piercing projectile passes through an entity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>enchanted / affected values</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>attacker</code></td><td>The entity holding the enchanted item</td></tr><tr><td><code>victim</code></td><td>The entity being attacked</td></tr><tr><td><code>damaging_entity</code></td><td>The direct source of damage (e.g. the arrow itself)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Not all combinations are valid for every component — <code>hit_block</code> has no <code>affected</code>, for example.</p>\n<h4>Single entry</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>post_attack:\n  enchanted: attacker\n  affected: victim\n  effect:\n    type: apply_mob_effect\n    to_apply: minecraft:poison\n    min_duration: 3.0\n    max_duration: 3.0\n    min_amplifier: 0.0\n    max_amplifier: 0.0\n  requirements:\n    condition: minecraft:random_chance\n    chance: 0.15</code></pre>\n<h4>Multiple entries</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>post_attack:\n  entries:\n    - enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: ignite\n        duration: 4.0\n    - enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: apply_mob_effect\n        to_apply: minecraft:slowness\n        min_duration: 2.0\n        max_duration: 2.0\n        min_amplifier: 1.0\n        max_amplifier: 1.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.3</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Entity effect types</h3>\n<p>These go inside the <code>effect:</code> block of an entity effect entry.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Entity_effects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity effects</a></p></blockquote>\n<h4>apply_mob_effect</h4>\n<p>Applies a potion effect to the target.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Effect#Effect_list\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Effect IDs</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: apply_mob_effect\n  to_apply: minecraft:poison        # required — effect ID or list of IDs\n  min_duration: 3.0                 # seconds (default 5.0)\n  max_duration: 3.0\n  min_amplifier: 0.0                # 0 = level I (default 0.0)\n  max_amplifier: 0.0</code></pre>\n<p><code>to_apply</code> can be a list for random selection:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>to_apply:\n  - minecraft:poison\n  - minecraft:wither</code></pre>\n<p>Duration and amplifier accept value providers:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>min_duration:\n  type: linear\n  base: 2.0\n  perLevel: 1.0\nmax_duration:\n  type: linear\n  base: 3.0\n  perLevel: 1.5</code></pre>\n<h4>ignite</h4>\n<p>Sets the target on fire.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: ignite\n  duration: 8.0    # seconds — accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>damage_entity</h4>\n<p>Deals direct damage.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Damage_type\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Damage types</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: damage_entity\n  damage_type: minecraft:generic    # required\n  min_damage: 1.0                   # accepts value providers\n  max_damage: 4.0</code></pre>\n<h4>change_item_damage</h4>\n<p>Damages the enchanted item&#x27;s durability.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: change_item_damage\n  amount: 1.0    # accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>apply_exhaustion</h4>\n<p>Drains the player&#x27;s food exhaustion meter.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: apply_exhaustion\n  amount: 0.1    # accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>apply_impulse</h4>\n<p>Applies a velocity impulse to the target.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: apply_impulse\n  direction: [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]          # [x, y, z] unit vector\n  coordinate_scale: [1.0, 0.0, 1.0]   # optional — scales each axis by a factor\n  magnitude: 2.0                        # accepts a value provider</code></pre>\n<h4>summon_entity</h4>\n<p>Spawns an entity at the target&#x27;s location.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Java_Edition_data_values#Entities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Entity IDs</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: summon_entity\n  entity: minecraft:lightning_bolt    # required — entity ID or list\n  join_team: false                    # optional</code></pre>\n<h4>run_function</h4>\n<p>Runs a datapack function.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: run_function\n  function: mynamespace:my_function    # required — function ID</code></pre>\n<h4>play_sound</h4>\n<p>Plays a sound at the target&#x27;s location.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Sounds.json#Sound_events\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sound events</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: play_sound\n  sound: minecraft:entity.lightning_bolt.thunder    # string or list for random pick\n  volume: 5.0    # accepts value providers\n  pitch: 1.0</code></pre>\n<p>Random sound pick:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>sound:\n  - minecraft:entity.lightning_bolt.thunder\n  - minecraft:entity.generic.explode</code></pre>\n<h4>spawn_particles</h4>\n<p>Spawns particles at the target.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Particles#Types_of_particles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Particle types</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: spawn_particles\n  particle:                      # required — particle definition (pass raw YAML)\n    type: minecraft:flame\n  horizontal_position:           # optional position/velocity sections\n    type: entity_position\n    offset: 0.5\n  vertical_position:\n    type: entity_position\n    offset: 0.5\n  speed: 0.1</code></pre>\n<h4>explode</h4>\n<p>Creates an explosion at the target.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: explode\n  radius: 3.0                          # accepts value provider\n  attribute_to_user: true              # optional\n  damage_type: minecraft:explosion     # optional\n  block_interaction: destroy           # optional: destroy | block | none | trigger_block\n  create_fire: false                   # optional\n  offset: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]             # optional [x, y, z]\n  immune_blocks: &#x27;#minecraft:dragon_immune&#x27;  # optional — block tag or list\n  knockback_multiplier: 1.0            # optional — value provider\n  sound: minecraft:entity.generic.explode   # optional</code></pre>\n<h4>replace_block</h4>\n<p>Replaces the block at the target location with another block state.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: replace_block\n  block_state:               # the replacement block state as raw YAML\n    Name: minecraft:ice\n  offset: [0.0, -1.0, 0.0]  # optional [x, y, z]\n  predicate:                 # optional block predicate\n    blocks: &#x27;#minecraft:water&#x27;\n  trigger_game_event: minecraft:block_change   # optional</code></pre>\n<h4>replace_disk</h4>\n<p>Same as <code>replace_block</code> but fills a disk area.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: replace_disk\n  block_state:\n    Name: minecraft:frosted_ice\n    Properties:\n      age: &#x27;0&#x27;\n  radius: 2.0          # accepts value provider\n  height: 1.0          # accepts value provider\n  offset: [0.0, -1.0, 0.0]</code></pre>\n<h4>set_block_properties</h4>\n<p>Changes properties of an existing block without replacing it.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: set_block_properties\n  properties:\n    waterlogged: &#x27;true&#x27;\n  offset: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n  trigger_game_event: minecraft:block_change</code></pre>\n<h4>all_of</h4>\n<p>Runs multiple effects together. Effects inside are all applied unconditionally (use outer <code>requirements</code> to gate the group).</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>effect:\n  type: all_of\n  effects:\n    - type: ignite\n      duration: 4.0\n    - type: apply_mob_effect\n      to_apply: minecraft:poison\n      min_duration: 2.0\n      max_duration: 2.0\n      min_amplifier: 0.0\n      max_amplifier: 0.0</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Attribute effects</h3>\n<p>Attribute modifiers change entity stat values while the enchanted item is equipped. Multiple modifiers are supported.</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attributes</a>, <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute#Modifiers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attribute modifiers</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>attributes:\n  - attribute: generic.attack_damage    # short alias or full minecraft:... ID\n    operation: add                      # add | add_multiplied_base | add_multiplied_total\n    value:\n      type: linear\n      base: 1.0\n      perLevel: 0.5\n    id: my_namespace:my_enchant/damage  # optional — auto-generated if omitted\n    requirements:                       # optional\n      condition: minecraft:random_chance\n      chance: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>Attribute operations</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>YAML value</th><th>Datapack value</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>add</code></td><td><code>add_value</code></td><td>Adds a flat amount to the base value</td></tr><tr><td><code>add_multiplied_base</code></td><td><code>add_multiplied_base</code></td><td>Adds <code>base × amount</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>add_multiplied_total</code></td><td><code>add_multiplied_total</code></td><td>Multiplies the running total</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Attribute#Operations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modifier operations</a></p></blockquote>\n<h4>Attribute short aliases</h4>\n<p>You can use short names instead of the full <code>minecraft:</code> ID:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Short alias</th><th>Full ID</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>damage</code>, <code>attack_damage</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.attack_damage</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>attack_speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.attack_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>armor</code>, <code>armor_points</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.armor</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>armor_toughness</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.armor_toughness</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>knockback_resistance</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.knockback_resistance</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>max_health</code>, <code>health</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.max_health</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>movement_speed</code>, <code>speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.movement_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>luck</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.luck</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>reach</code>, <code>block_reach</code>, <code>block_interaction_range</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.block_interaction_range</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>entity_reach</code>, <code>entity_interaction_range</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.entity_interaction_range</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>mining_efficiency</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.mining_efficiency</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>sneaking_speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.sneaking_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>submerged_mining_speed</code></td><td><code>minecraft:player.submerged_mining_speed</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>sweeping_damage_ratio</code>, <code>sweeping</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.sweeping_damage_ratio</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>armor_effectiveness</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.armor_effectiveness</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>gravity</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.gravity</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>jump_strength</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.jump_strength</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>safe_fall_distance</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.safe_fall_distance</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>fall_damage_multiplier</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.fall_damage_multiplier</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>burning_time</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.burning_time</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>explosion_knockback_resistance</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.explosion_knockback_resistance</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>water_movement_efficiency</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.water_movement_efficiency</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>oxygen_bonus</code></td><td><code>minecraft:generic.oxygen_bonus</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Any unrecognised alias is expanded to <code>minecraft:generic.&lt;alias&gt;</code> — so any future attributes added by Mojang will work automatically.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Flag components</h3>\n<p>Boolean toggles. Set to <code>true</code> to enable; <code>false</code> or omitting the key entirely disables (same result).</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#Flag_components\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Flag components</a></p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>damage_immunity</code></td><td>The enchanted item&#x27;s holder takes no damage from the effect&#x27;s damage type (e.g. Fire Protection vs fire)</td></tr><tr><td><code>prevent_equipment_drop</code></td><td>Mobs with this enchantment do not drop their equipment on death</td></tr><tr><td><code>prevent_armor_change</code></td><td>Players cannot equip or unequip armor while wearing this item</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>damage_immunity: true\nprevent_equipment_drop: true\nprevent_armor_change: true</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Special components</h3>\n<h4>crossbow_charging_sounds</h4>\n<p>Defines the sounds played per Quick Charge level while charging a crossbow. One entry per charge level (vanilla has 3).</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:crossbow_charging_sounds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">crossbow_charging_sounds</a></p></blockquote>\n<p>Full form (control both start and end sounds):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charging_sounds:\n  - start: minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_1\n    end: minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end\n  - start: minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_2\n    end: minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end\n  - start: minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_3\n    end: minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end</code></pre>\n<p>Shorthand (only specify start sounds; end always defaults to <code>minecraft:item.crossbow.loading_end</code>):</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>crossbow_charging_sounds:\n  - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_1\n  - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_2\n  - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_3</code></pre>\n<h4>trident_sound</h4>\n<p>Sounds played per Riptide level when spinning (one per level, vanilla has 3).</p>\n<blockquote><p>See: <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_definition#minecraft:trident_sound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">trident_sound</a></p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>trident_sound:\n  - minecraft:item.trident.riptide_1\n  - minecraft:item.trident.riptide_2\n  - minecraft:item.trident.riptide_3</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h3>Full examples</h3>\n<h4>Sharpness clone</h4>\n<p>Flat extra damage, grows with level.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>sharp_echo:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;7Sharp Echo&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 5\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: 1.0\n        perLevel: 0.5</code></pre>\n<h4>Fire-conditional damage boost</h4>\n<p>Extra damage only when the wielder is on fire.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>inferno_strike:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;cInferno Strike&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: 2.0\n        perLevel: 1.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n        entity: this\n        predicate:\n          minecraft:flags:\n            is_on_fire: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Stat-boosting ring (attribute modifiers)</h4>\n<p>Hypothetical ring item that boosts health and speed.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>vitality_ring:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;aVitality Ring&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [OFFHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#mythicenchants:enchantable/ring&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    attributes:\n      - attribute: max_health\n        operation: add\n        value:\n          type: linear\n          base: 2.0\n          perLevel: 2.0\n      - attribute: movement_speed\n        operation: add_multiplied_total\n        value:\n          type: constant\n          value: 0.05</code></pre>\n<h4>Poisoning strikes (entity effect)</h4>\n<p>Random chance to poison on hit.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>venom_touch:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;2Venom Touch&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    post_attack:\n      enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: apply_mob_effect\n        to_apply: minecraft:poison\n        min_duration:\n          type: linear\n          base: 1.0\n          perLevel: 1.0\n        max_duration:\n          type: linear\n          base: 2.0\n          perLevel: 1.0\n        min_amplifier: 0.0\n        max_amplifier: 0.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.25</code></pre>\n<h4>Multi-effect on hit (all_of)</h4>\n<p>Ignite and slow on hit, with a random chance gate.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>glacial_flare:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;bGlacial Flare&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 2\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    post_attack:\n      enchanted: attacker\n      affected: victim\n      effect:\n        type: all_of\n        effects:\n          - type: ignite\n            duration: 3.0\n          - type: apply_mob_effect\n            to_apply: minecraft:slowness\n            min_duration: 2.0\n            max_duration: 2.0\n            min_amplifier: 1.0\n            max_amplifier: 1.0\n      requirements:\n        condition: minecraft:random_chance\n        chance: 0.20</code></pre>\n<h4>Custom Quick Charge with sounds</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>swift_draw:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;eSwift Draw&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [MAINHAND]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/crossbow&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    crossbow_charge_time:\n      value:\n        type: linear\n        base: -0.25\n        perLevel: -0.25\n    crossbow_charging_sounds:\n      - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_1\n      - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_2\n      - minecraft:item.crossbow.quick_charge_3</code></pre>\n<h4>Protection with level-scaled damage reduction</h4>\n<p>Mimics vanilla Protection using <code>levels_squared</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>arcane_guard:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;9Arcane Guard&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 4\n  ValidSlots: [HEAD, CHEST, LEGS, FEET]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/armor&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage_protection:\n      value:\n        type: levels_squared\n        added: 1.0</code></pre>\n<h4>Multiple value effect entries (gated stacking)</h4>\n<p>Base reduction always applies; bonus kicks in only underwater.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>tide_ward:\n  Display: &#x27;&amp;3Tide Ward&#x27;\n  MaxLevel: 3\n  ValidSlots: [CHEST]\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/armor&#x27;\n  EnchantData:\n    damage_protection:\n      entries:\n        - value:\n            type: linear\n            base: 1.0\n            perLevel: 1.0\n        - value:\n            type: constant\n            value: 3.0\n          requirements:\n            condition: minecraft:entity_properties\n            entity: this\n            predicate:\n              minecraft:flags:\n                is_in_water: true</code></pre>"},"enchants:enchants/enchanting-table":{"h":"<p>Enchanting on the Enchanting Table is configured, and expanded, through these settings.  Global <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"table/enchanting\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Table/Enchanting\">Enchantment-Config</a> settings can affect this.  Just like in vanilla, <code>Treasure: true</code> enchantments are not offered on the table, intended only for external discovery like loot and trades.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10\n    MinCost: 15\n    MaxCost: 50\n    Promised: true\n    BookOffer: true\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n    Conditions:\n      - outside</code></pre>\n<h4>Weight</h4>\n<p>The likelihood of this enchantment being selected when offered by an enchanting table. Must be a whole number between 1 and 1024.\\ Higher values increase the chance of selection — values are weighed against all other enchantments, so keep weights in a similar range.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10</code></pre>\n<h4>MinCost &amp; MaxCost</h4>\n<p>The minimum and maximum modified enchantment levels required to roll this enchantment.\\ Accepts either a flat scalar value, or a <code>Base</code> + <code>PerLevel</code> breakdown for level-scaling costs.</p>\n<p>Scalar shorthand:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    MinCost: 15\n    MaxCost: 50</code></pre>\n<p>Base + per-level scaling:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    MinCost:\n      Base: 15\n      PerLevel: 9\n    MaxCost:\n      Base: 65\n      PerLevel: 0</code></pre>\n<h4>Promised</h4>\n<p>Determines whether this enchantment is ever shown as a named promise in the enchanting table tooltip. Defaults to <code>true</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Promised: true</code></pre>\n<h4>BookOffer</h4>\n<p>Determines whether books can be enchanted with this enchantment at the enchanting table. This is independent of <code>SupportedItems</code> and <code>PrimaryItems</code> — books are universally supported unless this is set to <code>false</code>. Defaults to <code>true</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    BookOffer: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Reagent</h4>\n<p>The reagent type(s) required for this enchantment to appear as a result at the enchanting table. Defaults to vanilla Lapis Lazuli only.\\ Accepts vanilla material IDs, MythicMobs/Crucible item IDs, or namespaced item model strings. Set to <code>ALL</code> to accept any reagent.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n      - moondust        # MythicMobs item ID\n      - nexo:sunshard   # namespaced item model string</code></pre>\n<h4>Conditions</h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/MythicMobs/-/wikis/Skills/conditions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MythicMobs conditions</a> evaluated at the location and time of opening the enchanting table. The enchantment will only be offered if all conditions pass.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Enchanting:\n    Conditions:\n      - outside\n      - (night || dusk)</code></pre>"},"enchants:enchants/enchantment-config":{"h":"<p>A complete outline of every enchantment configuration option, with defaults and descriptions.</p>\n<blockquote><p>This is <i>not</i> a plug-and-play enchantment, it is a complete reference of every element an enchantment config might contain.</p></blockquote>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n#  Full enchantment example — every supported field with REQUIRED / OPTIONAL notes\n#\n#  Place files like this in:\n#    plugins/MythicMobs/packs/&lt;yourpack&gt;/Enchantments/\n#\n#  Multiple enchantments per file are allowed. The top-level key is the enchant\n#  ID. Bare IDs (no colon) are namespaced automatically using the datapack name\n#  set in config.yml. Explicit namespaces (namespace:key) are used as-is.\n# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n# REQUIRED — enchantment ID. Bare IDs get the configured datapack namespace.\n#            Use namespace:key to pin it (e.g. mythicenchants:enchantment_id).\nenchantment_id:\n\n  # REQUIRED — display name shown in item lore. Supports &amp; color codes.\n  Display: &#x27;&lt;white&gt;Example Enchantment&#x27;\n\n  # OPTIONAL — extra lore line(s) shown below the enchant name. Defaults to empty.\n  Description: &#x27;&lt;gray&gt;The enchantment with all the options!&#x27;\n\n  # OPTIONAL — rarity tier. Controls enchanting-table weight grouping and\n  #            display color. One of: COMMON, UNCOMMON, RARE, VERY_RARE.\n  #            Defaults to COMMON.\n  Rarity: COMMON\n\n  # OPTIONAL — minimum enchantment level (for grading/display). Defaults to 1.\n  MinLevel: 1\n\n  # REQUIRED (effectively) — maximum level. Defaults to 1 if omitted.\n  MaxLevel: 1\n\n  # OPTIONAL — which equipment slots activate this enchant&#x27;s skills.\n  #            List one or more: MAINHAND, OFFHAND, HEAD, CHEST, LEGS, FEET, ALL.\n  #            Defaults to [ALL].\n  ValidSlots:\n    - ALL\n\n  # OPTIONAL — datapack item filter controlling which items can receive this\n  #            enchant. Accepts tag refs (#minecraft:enchantable/sword) or\n  #            individual item keys (minecraft:diamond_sword).\n  #            Defaults to #minecraft:enchantable/weapon.\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/weapon&#x27;\n\n  # OPTIONAL — items shown as &quot;primary&quot; in the datapack (affect enchanting table\n  #            cost weighting in vanilla logic). Usually left empty.\n  PrimaryItems: []\n\n  # OPTIONAL — XP level cost per merge step in an anvil. Defaults to 1.\n  AnvilCost: 1\n\n  # OPTIONAL — tag memberships. Unnamespaced tags get the plugin&#x27;s default\n  #            namespace. Tags drive conflict resolution and loot table filtering.\n  Tags:\n    - minecraft:on_random_loot  # appears in general vanilla chest/mob loot\n    - exclusive_damage          # example custom exclusion group\n\n  # OPTIONAL — enchantments (or #tag refs) that conflict with this one.\n  #            Conflicting enchants cannot coexist on the same item.\n  ConflictingEnchants:\n    - minecraft:sharpness\n    - minecraft:smite\n    - minecraft:bane_of_arthropods\n\n  # OPTIONAL — behaviour flags block. All three default to false/true as shown.\n  Options:\n    Enabled: true # whether available/obtainable or not and whether skills work\n    Cursed: false # Signifies whether a curse or no\n    Treasure: false # Signifies whether counted as a treasure enchantment\n    RandomLoot: true # Can be generated on random loot\n    Tradeable: true # can be traded by librarians\n    TradedEquipment: true # on traded equipment or no\n    MobSpawnEquipment: true # on mob equipment\n    TooltipOrder: 42 # weighted order of tool tip from 1 being the top\n  Enchanting:\n    # OPTIONAL — relative selection weight (higher = more likely to appear).\n    #            Defaults to 1\n    Weight: 1\n\n    # OPTIONAL — minimum modified enchantment level needed to roll this enchant.\n    #            Scalar shorthand: MinCost: 15  (Base only, PerLevel defaults to 0).\n    #            Full form shown below.\n    MinCost:\n      Base: 15        # minimum cost at level 1\n      PerLevel: 9     # added per level above 1 (so level 3 min = 15 + 9*2 = 33)\n\n    # OPTIONAL — maximum modified enchantment level that can still produce this\n    #            enchant. Same scalar / full-form rules as MinCost.\n    MaxCost:\n      Base: 65\n      PerLevel: 0\n\n    # OPTIONAL — whether this enchant can appear as a named promise hint in the\n    #            table tooltip. Defaults to true.\n    Promised: true\n\n    # OPTIONAL — whether this enchant can be enchanted onto books in the table.\n    #            Defaults to true, so only needs to be defined to prevent this.\n    BookOffer: true \n\n    # OPTIONAL — reagent(s) required in the lapis slot to unlock this enchant.\n    #            Omit entirely (or omit the list) = vanilla lapis only.\n    #            Single entry &quot;ALL&quot; = any reagent accepted.\n    #            Each entry is one of:\n    #              LAPIS_LAZULI          — plain vanilla lapis\n    #              &lt;crucible-id&gt;         — MythicCrucible item internal name\n    #              &lt;model-string-path&gt;   — custom model data string key\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n      - moondust        # also accepts this Crucible reagent\n      - nexo:sunshard   # can read any item model string on lapis items\n\n    # OPTIONAL — MythicMobs conditions evaluated when the table is opened.\n    #            This enchant only appears as an option when all conditions pass.\n    Conditions:\n      - (night || dusk)   # time-of-day condition\n      - outside           # player must be under open sky\n\n  # OPTIONAL — MythicMobs skill lines. Omit the block if this enchant has no\n  #            active skills (e.g. a pure datapack effect enchant).\n  #\n  #  Format:  mechanic{attributes} @targeter ~onTrigger\n  #\n  #  &lt;math:EXPR&gt; or for meta/sudo skills &lt;math.EXPR&gt; substitutes a computed value. Available variables:\n  #    enchant_level, enchant_maxlevel\n  #    player_health, player_max_health\n  #    target_health, target_max_health\n  #    fall_distance, \n  #    damage  (only on ~onDamaged)\n  #    item_attack  (only on ~onAttack)\n  #  Underscore and dash forms are both accepted (enchant_level = enchant-level).\n  Skills:\n    # Deal bonus damage scaled to enchantment level\n    - damage{a=&lt;math:enchant_level*1.5&gt;} @trigger ~onAttack\n\n    # Apply a timed weakness effect to the target, duration scales with level\n    - potion{type=WEAKNESS;d=&lt;math:enchant_level*40&gt;;amp=0} @trigger ~onAttack\n\n    # Reduce incoming projectile damage proportional to current level\n    - reducedamage{a=&lt;math:damage*0.05*enchant_level&gt;;cause=PROJECTILE} @self ~onDamaged\n\n    # Apply an attribute bonus while the item is equipped / remove it on unequip\n    - enchantattribute{attribute=ATTACK_DAMAGE;a=&lt;math:enchant_level*0.5&gt;;op=ADD_NUMBER;mode=APPLY} @self ~onEquip\n    - enchantattribute{attribute=ATTACK_DAMAGE;mode=REMOVE} @self ~onUnequip</code></pre>"},"enchants:enchants/enchantment-options":{"h":"<p>Additional options for configuring enchantments to various archetypes or behaviors.  Most behavior options are controlled by the enchantment&#x27;s <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Enchantment_tag_(Java_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Enchantment tags</a> in configuration.</p>\n<p>Options default to false unless defined otherwise on a config, and generally can be freely combined.</p>\n<h4>Enabled</h4>\n<p>If the enchantment is enabled at all.  Defaults to <code>true</code> so does not need to be present on active enchantments.</p>\n<p>An enchantment can be disabled with:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;red&gt;Disabled Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Enabled: false</code></pre>\n<h4>Cursed</h4>\n<p>Considered a curse enchantment, taking a red, ominous lore format and preventing grindstone removal:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Cursed: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Treasure</h4>\n<p>These items double their market price in villager trades:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    Treasure: true</code></pre>\n<h4>RandomLoot</h4>\n<p>These Enchantments will appear in dungeon/chest loot:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    RandomLoot: true</code></pre>\n<h4>Tradeable</h4>\n<p>These enchantments will appear on villager book trades:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n   Tradeable: true</code></pre>\n<h4>TradedEquipment</h4>\n<p>These enchantments will appear on villager-tradded gear:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    TradedEquipment: true</code></pre>\n<h4>MobSpawnEquipment</h4>\n<p>These enchantments will appear on mob equipment:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    MobSpawnEquipment: true</code></pre>\n<h4>TooltipOrder</h4>\n<p>Order of enchantments on the tooltip:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  Options:\n    TooltipOrder: 42</code></pre>"},"enchants:enchants/mythicstats":{"h":"<hr>\n<p>title: MythicStats</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>MythicAttributes|MythicStats</h3>\n<p>The <code>MythicAttributes|MythicStats|Stats</code> section is a declarative shorthand for applying MythicMobs stat modifiers without writing full skill line syntax. Each entry generates a pair of synthetic skill lines — one on <code>~onEquip</code> to apply the modifier, and one on <code>~onUnequip</code> to remove it.</p>\n<p>Unlike <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/attributes\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes\">Attributes</a>, which writes modifiers into item metadata (visible in tooltips, persistent), <code>MythicAttributes|MythicStats|Stats</code> applies modifiers directly to the entity through MythicMobs&#x27; stat system. They are transient — not stored on the item, not visible in the tooltip, and re-applied whenever the item is equipped. You&#x27;ll notice through the Page We use Stats, MythicStats, or MythicAttributes, Either is applicable as one is an Alias of the other.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MythicStats:\n    - &lt;STAT&gt; &lt;AMOUNT&gt; [TYPE]</code></pre>\n<p>Each line follows this format:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>STAT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The MythicMobs stat name (see <span class=\"ilink\">Stats</span>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AMOUNT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>A numeric value or <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expression</td></tr><tr><td><code>TYPE</code></td><td>No</td><td>The modifier type (see <span class=\"ilink\">Types</span>). Defaults to <code>ADDITIVE</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Example</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>example_enchant:\n  Display: &quot;&lt;yellow&gt;Example Enchant&quot;\n  MythicAttributes:\n    - POWER 10\n    - CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE 5\n    - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;\n    - MOVEMENT_SPEED 0.1 ADDITIVE_MULTIPLIER</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h4>Stats</h4>\n<p>These are the built-in stats registered by MythicMobs. Custom stats defined in your MythicMobs configuration are also valid.</p>\n<h5>Damage</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>BONUS_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Flat bonus added to outgoing damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>PERCENT_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Percentage bonus to outgoing damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to land a critical hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>CRITICAL_STRIKE_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Multiplier applied on a critical hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>CRITICAL_STRIKE_RESILIENCE</code></td><td>Reduces incoming critical hit damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>DODGE_NEGATION</code></td><td>Reduces target&#x27;s chance to dodge</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_NEGATION</code></td><td>Reduces target&#x27;s chance to parry</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Defense</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>DEFENSE</code></td><td>Flat damage reduction</td></tr><tr><td><code>DAMAGE_REDUCTION</code></td><td>Percentage damage reduction</td></tr><tr><td><code>DODGE_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to completely avoid an attack</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to parry an attack</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_POWER</code></td><td>Damage reduction when a parry triggers</td></tr><tr><td><code>PARRY_COUNTERATTACK</code></td><td>Damage dealt on a successful parry</td></tr><tr><td><code>HEALTH_REGENERATION</code></td><td>Passive health regeneration</td></tr><tr><td><code>LIFESTEAL_CHANCE</code></td><td>Chance to lifesteal on hit</td></tr><tr><td><code>LIFESTEAL_POWER</code></td><td>Amount of health restored on lifesteal</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>General</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POWER</code></td><td>General power stat used in skill scaling</td></tr><tr><td><code>LOOT_BIAS</code></td><td>Influences loot roll outcomes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Vanilla (mapped to Bukkit attributes)</h5>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ATTACK_DAMAGE</code></td><td>Melee attack damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>ATTACK_SPEED</code></td><td>Attack speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>HEALTH</code></td><td>Maximum health</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR</code></td><td>Armor points</td></tr><tr><td><code>ARMOR_TOUGHNESS</code></td><td>Armor toughness</td></tr><tr><td><code>MOVEMENT_SPEED</code></td><td>Movement speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>FLYING_SPEED</code></td><td>Flying speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>KNOCKBACK_RESISTANCE</code></td><td>Resistance to knockback</td></tr><tr><td><code>FOLLOW_RANGE</code></td><td>Entity follow/detection range</td></tr><tr><td><code>SCALE</code></td><td>Entity scale</td></tr><tr><td><code>STEP_HEIGHT</code></td><td>Step height (auto-climb)</td></tr><tr><td><code>JUMP_STRENGTH</code></td><td>Jump strength</td></tr><tr><td><code>GRAVITY</code></td><td>Gravity multiplier</td></tr><tr><td><code>SAFE_FALL_DISTANCE</code></td><td>Distance before fall damage begins</td></tr><tr><td><code>FALL_DAMAGE_MULTIPLIER</code></td><td>Multiplier applied to fall damage</td></tr><tr><td><code>BLOCK_BREAK_SPEED</code></td><td>Block breaking speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>BLOCK_INTERACTION_RANGE</code></td><td>Block interaction reach</td></tr><tr><td><code>ENTITY_INTERACTION_RANGE</code></td><td>Entity interaction reach</td></tr><tr><td><code>MOVEMENT_EFFICIENCY</code></td><td>Movement efficiency on slow blocks</td></tr><tr><td><code>SNEAKING_SPEED</code></td><td>Movement speed while sneaking</td></tr><tr><td><code>WATER_MOVEMENT_EFFICIENCY</code></td><td>Movement efficiency in water</td></tr><tr><td><code>OXYGEN_BONUS</code></td><td>Bonus oxygen/breath</td></tr><tr><td><code>BURNING_TIME</code></td><td>Duration of fire on entity</td></tr><tr><td><code>EXPLOSION_KNOCKBACK_RESISTANCE</code></td><td>Resistance to explosion knockback</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h4>Modifier Types</h4>\n<p>Controls how the amount is applied relative to the entity&#x27;s base stat value.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ADDITIVE</code></td><td>Adds a flat value to the stat. Default.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADDITIVE_MULTIPLIER</code></td><td>Multiplies the base stat — e.g. <code>0.1</code> = +10%</td></tr><tr><td><code>COMPOUND_MULTIPLIER</code></td><td>Multiplies the running total including other multipliers</td></tr><tr><td><code>SETTER</code></td><td>Overrides the stat to the exact value</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h4>Math Expressions</h4>\n<p>The <code>AMOUNT</code> field supports <code>&lt;math:&gt;</code> expressions for level-scaling modifiers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  Stats:\n    - ATTACK_DAMAGE &lt;math:enchant_level*2&gt;\n    - CRITICAL_STRIKE_CHANCE &lt;math:enchant_level*3&gt;\n    - MOVEMENT_SPEED &lt;math:enchant_level*0.02&gt; ADDITIVE_MULTIPLIER</code></pre>\n<p>All standard enchantment variables are available: <code>enchant_level</code>, <code>enchant_maxlevel</code>, etc.</p>\n<hr>\n<h4>Notes</h4>\n<ul><li>Modifiers are identified internally by a stable source key derived from the enchant ID and stat name, ensuring the correct modifier is always removed on unequip.</li><li>Because modifiers are transient, they are lost on server restart and re-applied the next time the item is equipped.</li><li>Unknown stat names will log a warning and produce no effect.</li><li>For item-level attribute modifiers that appear in the item tooltip and persist on the item, use <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/attributes\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Attributes\">Attributes</a> instead.</li></ul>\n<hr>\n<h4>Comparison: Attributes vs MythicStats</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><code>Attributes</code></th><th><code>MythicStats</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mechanic</td><td><code>enchantitemattribute</code></td><td><code>playerstat</code></td></tr><tr><td>System</td><td>Bukkit attribute API</td><td>MythicMobs stat system</td></tr><tr><td>Stored on</td><td>Item metadata</td><td>Entity (transient)</td></tr><tr><td>Visible in tooltip</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Persists across relog</td><td>Yes</td><td>Reapplied on login</td></tr><tr><td>Slot group</td><td>Required</td><td>Not applicable</td></tr><tr><td>Triggers</td><td><code>~onEnchant</code> / <code>~onEnchantRemove</code></td><td><code>~onEquip</code> / <code>~onUnequip</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>`</code></p>"},"enchants:vanilla/vanilla-enchantments":{"h":"<p>MythicEnchants can manage, modify and overwrite vanilla enchantments thanks to its modern data-driven approach.  These can be found in <code>plugins/MythicMobs/packs/Vanilla_Enchants/enchantments/</code> and can be fully customized just like any <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/custom-enchantments\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Custom-Enchantments\">custom enchantment</a>, overriding vanilla enchants of the same names.</p>\n<h3>Examples:</h3>\n<p>📝 <code>Config</code></p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>MENDING:\n  MaxLevel: 1</code></pre>"},"enchants:table/enchanting":{"h":"<p>MythicEnchants manages the vanilla <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/enchanting_table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">enchanting table</a>&#x27;s offerings while adding features such as live conditional enchanting using <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchanting-table\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table\">enchantment conditions</a> and new <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"table/reagents\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Table/Reagents\">reagent types</a> beyond <a href=\"https://minecraft.wiki/w/Lapis_lazuli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lapis Lazuli</a>.</p>\n<h3>Enchanting Table Plugin Configuration</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"info/config\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/info/config\">Plugin&#x27;s Config</a> features a section dedicated to global enchanting table behavior, managing the vanilla table with a variety of options when <code>custom-table: true</code>.  (Without MythicEnchants table management, many features such as reagents and enchanting conditions will not take effect).</p>\n<p>The configuration options are explained in comments in the config file itself.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>enchanting:\n  # Disables MythicEnchants providing its own emulated enchanting table.\n  # Required for reagents and conditional enchanting.\n  # All enchantments are registered using vanilla datapack offering settings.\n  custom-table: true\n  # Vanilla-override: register treasure enchants as offered in the table.\n  allow-treasure: false\n  # Whether vanilla enchantments can appear in the custom enchanting table.\n  # When false (default), only custom MythicEnchants enchantments are offered.\n  # When true, vanilla enchantments are filtered using datapack supported_items\n  # tags (authoritative item-type check) and can fill slots that have no custom\n  # enchantment available.\n  vanilla-in-table: true\n  # When true, an empty reagent slot is treated as if vanilla lapis were\n  # present — offers are computed against the &quot;vanilla&quot; reagent bucket and\n  # shown immediately when the player drops in an item. When false (default),\n  # the table waits until the player adds *something* to the reagent slot\n  # before producing offers (vanilla lapis still rolls vanilla-bucket offers,\n  # custom reagents roll their own bucket). Use `true` for the legacy\n  # always-show behavior; `false` for a reagent-gated UX.\n  assume-reagent-lapis: false\n  # Custom-table only. Replaces vanilla&#x27;s hard-coded &quot;1 power per bookshelf,\n  # capped at 15&quot; with a configurable material weight map and three per-slot\n  # equations evaluated against a `count` variable.\n  #\n  #   * `materials` — block ID → power weight. Any block listed here is counted\n  #                   at the same 30 positions vanilla scans for bookshelves.\n  #                   The value is summed (e.g. 5 BOOKSHELF + 2 EMERALD_BLOCK\n  #                   with the weights below → count = 5*1 + 2*3 = 11).\n  #   * `require-line-of-sight` — when true, follows vanilla&#x27;s air-gap rule\n  #                   (the cell between the table and a power block must be\n  #                   air). Stops players cheesing with solid walls.\n  #   * `equations` — exp4j expressions for slot1/slot2/slot3 (top→bottom in\n  #                   the table UI). Variable `count` is the summed power.\n  #                   Functions: `floor`, `ceil`, `min`, `max`, `clamp`,\n  #                   `randomInt(a,b)` (inclusive), plus all standard math.\n  #                   Omit a slot&#x27;s equation to fall back to the vanilla\n  #                   formula for that slot.</code></pre>\n<p>Bookshelves are the vanilla conduit block used for Enchantment power to increase the enchantment levels and offers.</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>  table-power:\n    materials:\n      BOOKSHELF: 1\n      # EMERALD_BLOCK: 3\n    require-line-of-sight: true\n    # Optional. When omitted, scans vanilla&#x27;s hand-picked 30 positions (the\n    # exact set vanilla uses for bookshelves). When present, replaces that\n    # with a chebyshev-distance cuboid scan around the table.\n    #\n    #   inner — exclusive lower bound on max(|dx|,|dz|). 2 reproduces vanilla&#x27;s\n    #           &quot;shelves can&#x27;t be adjacent to the table&quot; gap. 0 lets blocks\n    #           directly touching the table count.\n    #   outer — inclusive upper bound on max(|dx|,|dz|).\n    #   y-min / y-max — inclusive Y offsets relative to the table block.\n    #                   Vanilla equivalent is 0..1 (two layers).\n    #\n    # LOS rule for wide radii: there&#x27;s no single &quot;cell between table and shelf&quot;\n    # once the radius exceeds 2, so the check approximates by requiring the\n    # cell at (sign(dx), 0, sign(dz)) — the doorway adjacent to the table —\n    # to be replaceable. Solid wall around the table still kills the bonus.\n    # radius:\n    #   inner: 2\n    #   outer: 7\n    #   y-min: 0\n    #   y-max: 1\n    equations:\n      slot1: &quot;floor(min(max((randomInt(1,8)+floor(count/2)+randomInt(0,count))/6, 1), 10))&quot;\n      slot2: &quot;floor(min((((randomInt(1,8)+floor(count/2)+randomInt(0,count))*2)/4)+1, 15))&quot;\n      slot3: &quot;floor(max(((randomInt(1,8)+floor(count/2)+randomInt(0,count))/2)+2, min(20, count*2)))&quot;\n    # After each slot&#x27;s equation evaluates, clamp the result to this maximum.\n    # Saves wrapping every equation in min(...). Defaults shown below\n    # (10/15/30) mirror vanilla&#x27;s progression. To opt a slot out of its cap\n    # so only the global `max-base-level` applies, set it to `0`. Omitting\n    # the entire block keeps the defaults; omitting a single slot also\n    # keeps that slot&#x27;s default.\n    slot-caps:\n      slot1: 10\n      slot2: 15\n      slot3: 30\n    #\n    # Hard upper bound applied last — defaults to 30 to match vanilla&#x27;s\n    # enchanting-table UI. Lifting beyond 30 works (the algorithm will pick\n    # higher-tier enchants for the candidate pool) but the XP-cost number\n    # renders in red and demands that many player levels to confirm. Set\n    # carefully if you want deeper progression than vanilla allows.\n    max-base-level: 30</code></pre>\n<h3>Enchanting Configuration for Enchantments</h3>\n<p><a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/custom-enchantments\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Custom-Enchantments\">Enchantments</a> can have their Enchanting Table behavior <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"enchants/enchanting-table\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Enchants/Enchanting-Table\">configured directly</a>.</p>"},"enchants:table/reagents":{"h":"<h2>Reagents</h2>\n<h3>Overview</h3>\n<p>Reagents are items placed in the enchanting table&#x27;s lapis slot that control which enchantments appear and how table power scales. Instead of only using vanilla Lapis Lazuli, you can define custom reagent items — such as MythicCrucible items or custom model data lapis — to gate specific enchantments behind specific reagent types.</p>\n<blockquote><p>Reagents require <code>custom-table: true</code> in <a href=\"#\" class=\"wl\" data-p=\"config/config.yml\" data-x=\"https://git.mythiccraft.io/mythiccraft/mythicenchants/-/wikis/Config/config.yml\">config.yml</a> to function.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>How Reagents Work</h3>\n<ol><li>A player places an item in the enchanting table&#x27;s lapis slot</li><li>MythicEnchants resolves the item to a <b>reagent key</b> using a <span class=\"ilink\">priority-based matcher</span></li><li>The enchantment pool is filtered to only show enchantments that accept that reagent</li><li>Table power equations may be overridden per-reagent to modify slot costs</li></ol>\n<p>Reagent items are <b>consumed</b> — they are read to determine which enchantments to offer, similar to how vanilla uses lapis.</p>\n<h3>Defining Reagents</h3>\n<p>Reagent files are loaded from:</p>\n<ul><li><code>plugins/MythicMobs/Packs/&lt;pack&gt;/Reagents/</code> (pack overlays, loaded second — can override base entries)</li></ul>\n<p>Each YAML file can declare multiple reagents as top-level keys. File names are cosmetic.</p>\n<h4>Structure</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>moondust:\n  matches:\n    mythiccrucible: moondust\n    model-strings:\n      - nexo:item/material/moondust\n    legacy-model-data: 1042\n  table-power:\n    mode: override\n    equations:\n      slot1: &quot;floor(min(count*1.5, 12))&quot;\n      slot2: null\n      slot3: &quot;floor(count*2)&quot;\n    slot-caps:\n      slot1: 12\n      slot3: 35\n    max-base-level: 35</code></pre>\n<h4>Matches Block</h4>\n<p>The <code>matches:</code> block defines how an item in the lapis slot is identified as this reagent.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mythiccrucible</code></td><td>MythicCrucible internal item name (also accepts <code>mythic</code> or <code>crucible</code> as the key)</td></tr><tr><td><code>model-strings</code></td><td>List of custom model data strings to match (case-insensitive)</td></tr><tr><td><code>legacy-model-data</code></td><td>Legacy integer custom model data value</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p>Non-vanilla reagents <b>must</b> have at least one matcher. The <code>vanilla</code> key is reserved and never needs matchers.</p></blockquote>\n<h4>Table Power Block</h4>\n<p>The optional <code>table-power:</code> block overrides global table power calculations for this reagent.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>override</code> replaces global equations; <code>additive</code> adds to them</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>equations</code></td><td>Per-slot math expressions (<code>slot1</code>, <code>slot2</code>, <code>slot3</code>). Use <code>null</code> to inherit global. Variable <code>count</code> is the power value</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>slot-caps</code></td><td>Per-slot upper bounds applied after the equation</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>max-base-level</code></td><td>Hard ceiling on the computed base level (overrides global)</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h5>Table Power Resolution Order</h5>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>1. Compute global base value (global equation or vanilla formula)\n2. Apply reagent override/additive:\n   - OVERRIDE: replace with reagent equation (or keep global if null)\n   - ADDITIVE: add reagent equation result to global\n3. Apply cap: min(result, reagent cap or global cap)\n4. Apply ceiling: min(result, reagent ceiling or global ceiling or 30)\n5. Clamp to minimum of 1</code></pre>\n<h3>Using Reagents in Enchantments</h3>\n<p>In an enchantment&#x27;s <code>Enchanting:</code> block, the <code>Reagent</code> list controls which reagents unlock that enchantment at the table:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>LunarLight:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 5\n    Reagent:\n      - moondust\n      - starshard</code></pre>\n<h4>Special Values</h4>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code></td><td>Vanilla lapis with no metadata (also <code>LAPIS</code> or <code>VANILLA</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ALL</code></td><td>Enchantment appears for <b>any</b> reagent (also <code>*</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><i>(omitted)</i></td><td>If <code>Reagent</code> is not specified, defaults to vanilla lapis only</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Examples</h4>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code># Only appears with moondust reagent\nLunarEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 10\n    Reagent:\n      - moondust\n\n# Appears with any reagent\nUniversalEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 5\n    Reagent:\n      - ALL\n\n# Appears with vanilla lapis or a specific custom item\nHybridEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 8\n    Reagent:\n      - LAPIS_LAZULI\n      - starshard\n\n# No Reagent field = vanilla lapis only (default behavior)\nBasicEnchant:\n  Enchanting:\n    Weight: 15</code></pre>\n<h3>Item Resolution Order</h3>\n<p>When a player places an item in the lapis slot, MythicEnchants resolves it to a reagent key using this priority:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Method</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><b>Declared reagent matchers</b> — checks <code>mythiccrucible</code>, <code>model-strings</code>, and <code>legacy-model-data</code> fields in order</td><td><code>moondust</code> (via Crucible internal name)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><b>Plain vanilla lapis</b> — <code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code> material with no custom metadata</td><td><code>vanilla</code></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><b>MythicCrucible API lookup</b> — queries MythicBukkit for the item&#x27;s internal name</td><td><code>starshard</code></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Custom model string</b> — reads Paper&#x27;s <code>CustomModelDataComponent</code> first string value</td><td><code>nexo:item/material/gem</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Vanilla Reagent Override</h3>\n<p>The reserved <code>vanilla</code> key lets you override table power for plain lapis without needing matchers:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>vanilla:\n  table-power:\n    mode: additive\n    equations:\n      slot1: &quot;1&quot;\n      slot2: &quot;1&quot;\n      slot3: &quot;1&quot;</code></pre>\n<h3>Supported Reagent Types</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Matcher Field</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vanilla Lapis Lazuli</td><td>Standard <code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code> material</td><td>Automatic (keyword <code>LAPIS_LAZULI</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>MythicCrucible Items</td><td>Items created by MythicCrucible</td><td><code>mythiccrucible</code></td></tr><tr><td>Custom Model Data Strings</td><td>Items with Paper <code>CustomModelDataComponent</code> strings</td><td><code>model-strings</code></td></tr><tr><td>Legacy Custom Model Data</td><td>Items with integer custom model data</td><td><code>legacy-model-data</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Config Settings</h3>\n<p>These settings in <code>config.yml</code> affect reagent behavior:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>enchanting:\n  custom-table: true              # Must be true for reagents to work\n  assume-reagent-lapis: false     # false = wait for reagent in slot before showing offers\n                                  # true = show vanilla-eligible offers even with empty slot</code></pre>"},"enchants:datapack/tags":{"h":"<h3>Custom datapack tags</h3>\n<p>You can define your own datapack tags from YAML and have MythicEnchants generate the JSON into the installed datapack. Put files at:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>&lt;MythicMobs pack&gt;/datapack/&lt;namespace&gt;/tags/&lt;registry&gt;/&lt;file&gt;.yml</code></pre>\n<ul><li><code>&lt;namespace&gt;</code> — the tag&#x27;s namespace (e.g. <code>mythicenchants</code>, <code>minecraft</code>).</li><li><code>&lt;registry&gt;</code> — the vanilla tag registry. <b><code>item</code></b> is supported today; the system is registry-keyed, so other registries can be added later by dropping files in their folder.</li></ul>\n<p>Each file declares one tag. Two shapes:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>farming_tools:                 # full form\n  replace: false\n  values:\n    - &quot;#minecraft:hoes&quot;        # tag reference (passed through)\n    - minecraft:shears         # material (bare DIAMOND_HOE or namespaced both work)\n    - mythic:Fire_Axe          # MythicMobs/Crucible item → resolved to its BASE MATERIAL\n\nmining_special:                # shorthand: a bare value list (replace = false)\n  - DIAMOND_PICKAXE\n  - mythic:Crucible_Drill</code></pre>\n<p>Generated to <code>data/&lt;namespace&gt;/tags/item/&lt;key&gt;.json</code>. Reference the tag anywhere a tag is accepted, e.g. <code>SupportedItems: &#x27;#mythicenchants:farming_tools&#x27;</code> or in <code>PrimaryItems</code>. Tags with the same id across multiple packs are merged. Unknown materials / unresolvable <code>mythic:</code> items are skipped with a warning (the rest of the tag still generates).</p>\n<blockquote><p><b><code>mythic:</code> resolves to a material, not the exact item.</b> Datapack tags match by item type, so <code>mythic:Fire_Axe</code> contributes its base material (e.g. <code>netherite_axe</code>) — the tag then matches <i>all</i> netherite axes. To restrict an enchant to the <b>specific</b> Mythic/Crucible item, see <i>StrictMythicItems</i> below.</p></blockquote>\n<h3>Restricting an enchant to a specific Mythic/Crucible item</h3>\n<p>Add <code>mythic:&lt;id&gt;</code> entries to <code>PrimaryItems</code> and set <code>StrictMythicItems: true</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"cb\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><code>my_crucible_enchant:\n  SupportedItems: &#x27;#minecraft:enchantable/sharp_weapon&#x27;\n  PrimaryItems: [&#x27;mythic:Fire_Axe&#x27;]\n  Options:\n    StrictMythicItems: true     # (top-level StrictMythicItems: true also works)</code></pre>\n<p>With the flag on, the enchant can only be applied to the exact Mythic item(s) listed — enforced at runtime on the enchanting table, anvil, the <code>enchant{}</code> mechanic, and the <code>applyEnchantment</code> API. Without <code>mythic:</code> entries the flag is a no-op. (The datapack still only knows the material, so this runtime check is what makes the restriction exact.)</p>"}});
